    <sense id="ciŋ_216_s1">
      <grammatical-info value="Adverb"/>
      <gloss lang="fr"><text>clairement, de ses propres yeux (cɔu ciŋ, a lehɔl ciŋ)</text></gloss>
      <gloss lang="en"><text>clearly, with one's own eyes (cɔu ciŋ, a lehɔl ciŋ)</text></gloss>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="2.3.1 See"/>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="9.2.2 Adverbs"/>
    </sense>
    <note type="source"><form lang="en"><text>BKG: 32 occurrences, first GEN.45.12</text></form></note>
  </entry>
  <entry id="ciŋaa_217">
    <lexical-unit><form lang="kqs"><text>ciŋaa</text></form></lexical-unit>
    <trait name="status" value="check"/>
    <variant><form lang="kqs"><text>ciŋa</text></form></variant>
    <sense id="ciŋaa_217_s1">
      <grammatical-info value="Verb"/>
      <gloss lang="fr"><text>disposer, arranger (le bois) ; attiser (le feu) ; atteindre (un total)</text></gloss>
      <gloss lang="en"><text>lay, arrange (wood); stoke (a fire); reach (a total)</text></gloss>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="7.5.9 Put"/>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="5.5 Fire"/>
    </sense>
    <field type="southern-kissi-sense"><form lang="en"><text>join the edges of, push together; put one's mouth to a cup, drink; stoke a fire; argue in court; add money to a partial payment</text></form></field>
    <note type="source"><form lang="en"><text>Childs 2000, p. 49: cìŋàá</text></form></note>
    <note><form lang="fr"><text>yinnden ciŋaa « faire du feu » (Es 40,16) ; vɔsila lan la ciŋa kɛmɛ lehiɔɔlu a beleyaa « au bout de 430 ans » (Ex 12,41). ciŋan : má ciŋan le kolɔɔ « ils se penchèrent pour boire » (Jg 7,6).</text></form></note>
  </entry>
  <entry id="ciŋiipianduei_218">
    <lexical-unit><form lang="kqs"><text>ciŋiipianduei</text></form></lexical-unit>
