    <note type="source"><form lang="en"><text>BKG: 1 occurrences, first EZK.4.9; Keita 1979, p. 140: Työnndon; Childs 2000, p. 58: cɔ̀ɔ́ŋndé</text></form></note>
  </entry>
  <entry id="cɔnɔnndo_277">
    <lexical-unit><form lang="kqs"><text>cɔnɔnndo</text></form></lexical-unit>
    <trait name="status" value="attested"/>
    <variant><form lang="kqs"><text>cɔn</text></form></variant>
    <variant><form lang="kqs"><text>can</text></form></variant>
    <variant><form lang="kqs"><text>cen</text></form></variant>
    <variant><form lang="kqs"><text>cɔnnun</text></form></variant>
    <sense id="cɔnɔnndo_277_s1">
      <grammatical-info value="Verb"/>
      <gloss lang="fr"><text>se lever, partir</text></gloss>
      <gloss lang="en"><text>get up, set out</text></gloss>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="7.1.1 Stand"/>
    </sense>
    <field type="southern-kissi-sense"><form lang="en"><text>get up, arise; grow</text></form></field>
    <note type="source"><form lang="en"><text>BKG: 200 occurrences, first GEN.5; Keita 1979, p. 116: Työnönndo; Childs 2000, p. 57: cɔ̀ŋɔ̀ɔ́</text></form></note>
    <note><form lang="fr"><text>cen : radical négatif (GEN 31,35).</text></form></note>
  </entry>
  <entry id="cɔu_278">
    <lexical-unit><form lang="kqs"><text>cɔu</text></form></lexical-unit>
    <trait name="status" value="attested"/>
    <variant><form lang="kqs"><text>ca</text></form></variant>
    <variant><form lang="kqs"><text>ce</text></form></variant>
    <variant><form lang="kqs"><text>ci</text></form></variant>
    <variant><form lang="kqs"><text>cɔ</text></form></variant>
    <variant><form lang="kqs"><text>canin</text></form></variant>
    <sense id="cɔu_278_s1">
      <grammatical-info value="Verb"/>
      <gloss lang="fr"><text>voir</text></gloss>
      <gloss lang="en"><text>see</text></gloss>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="2.3.1 See"/>
    </sense>
    <field type="southern-kissi-sense"><form lang="en"><text>see, perceive, think</text></form></field>
    <note type="source"><form lang="en"><text>BKG: 382 occurrences, first GEN.2.19; Keita 1979, p. 116: Työw; Childs 2000, p. 58: cɔ̀ɔ́</text></form></note>
    <note><form lang="fr"><text>Keita écrit työw ; la Bible écrit cɔu (GEN 2,19 ; 13,15) ; cɔw y signifie « créer ». ci : radical négatif (GEN 31,33). Verbe à alternance : ca, ce (accompli), cɔ, ci (négatif), canin (futur).</text></form></note>
  </entry>
  <entry id="cɔvɔɔ_279">
