    <sense id="kɔngɔ_910_s1">
      <grammatical-info value="Noun"/>
      <gloss lang="fr"><text>terre ferme ; rive, bord (de l'eau)</text></gloss>
      <gloss lang="en"><text>dry land; shore, bank</text></gloss>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="1.2.1 Land"/>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="8.6.6 Edge"/>
    </sense>
    <field type="southern-kissi-sense"><form lang="en"><text>bank, shore, dry land; higher ground around a swamp</text></form></field>
    <note type="source"><form lang="en"><text>BKG: 181 occurrences, first GEN.1.9; Childs 2000, p. 185: kɔ̀ŋgɔ́ɔ</text></form></note>
  </entry>
  <entry id="kɔngɔlanndo_911">
    <lexical-unit><form lang="kqs"><text>kɔngɔlanndo</text></form></lexical-unit>
    <trait name="status" value="attested"/>
    <variant><form lang="kqs"><text>kɔngɔlan</text></form></variant>
    <sense id="kɔngɔlanndo_911_s1">
      <grammatical-info value="Verb"/>
      <gloss lang="fr"><text>projeter, avoir l'intention de ; chercher à (nuire)</text></gloss>
      <gloss lang="en"><text>plan, intend; seek (to harm)</text></gloss>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="3.3.1 Decide, plan"/>
    </sense>
    <note type="source"><form lang="en"><text>BKG: 13 occurrences, first GEN.27.42</text></form></note>
    <note><form lang="fr"><text>Esau … co kɔngɔlanndo le pɔmbɔ ndɔ diyɔɔ « Ésaü projette de tuer son frère » (Gn 27,42) ; Mɛlɛka kɔngɔlan le kobio ho tɛɛmbuuo (Gn 19,14). Homographe : kɔngɔlan, pluriel de kɔngɔɔ « rive ».</text></form></note>
  </entry>
  <entry id="kɔngɔlɔɛi_912">
    <lexical-unit><form lang="kqs"><text>kɔngɔlɔɛi</text></form></lexical-unit>
    <trait name="noun-class" value="i"/>
    <trait name="status" value="check"/>
    <sense id="kɔngɔlɔɛi_912_s1">
      <grammatical-info value="Noun"/>
      <gloss lang="fr"><text>tactique (Keita)</text></gloss>
      <gloss lang="en"><text>tactic (Keita)</text></gloss>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="4.8.3 War"/>
    </sense>
    <field type="southern-kissi-sense"><form lang="en"><text>long war sword (about four feet)</text></form></field>
    <note type="source"><form lang="en"><text>Keita 1979, p. 156: Köngölöèi; Childs 2000, p. 253: mùɛ̀-kɔ́ŋgɔ̀lúɛ́í</text></form></note>
    <note><form lang="fr"><text>Sens à confirmer : chez Childs, kɔ́ŋgɔ̀lúɛ́í désigne une grande épée de guerre.</text></form></note>
  </entry>
  <entry id="kɔngɔɔ_913">
    <lexical-unit><form lang="kqs"><text>kɔngɔɔ</text></form></lexical-unit>
    <trait name="noun-class" value="o"/>
    <trait name="status" value="attested"/>
    <sense id="kɔngɔɔ_913_s1">
      <grammatical-info value="Noun"/>
      <gloss lang="fr"><text>rivage, rive, bord</text></gloss>
      <gloss lang="en"><text>shore, bank, edge</text></gloss>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="1.3.1 Bodies of water"/>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="8.6.6 Edge"/>
    </sense>
    <field type="southern-kissi-sense"><form lang="en"><text>bank, shore, dry land; the higher ground around a swamp</text></form></field>
    <note type="source"><form lang="en"><text>BKG: 32 occurrences, first GEN.41.2; Keita 1979, p. 155: Köngöö; Childs 2000, p. 185: kɔ̀ŋgɔ́ɔ́</text></form></note>
  </entry>
  <entry id="kɔnndan_914">
    <lexical-unit><form lang="kqs"><text>kɔnndan</text></form></lexical-unit>
    <trait name="status" value="attested"/>
    <sense id="kɔnndan_914_s1">
      <grammatical-info value="Noun"/>
      <gloss lang="fr"><text>départ, fuite</text></gloss>
      <gloss lang="en"><text>departure, flight</text></gloss>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="7.2.3 Move toward something"/>
    </sense>
    <note type="source"><form lang="en"><text>BKG: 84 occurrences, first GEN.15.2</text></form></note>
    <note><form lang="fr"><text>can kɔnndan « s'enfuir, partir » (Gn 31,20) ; mal … kɔnndan « laisser partir » (Ex 14,5) ; a va kɔnndan-ndo « ils étaient en route » (Ex 12,38).</text></form></note>
  </entry>
  <entry id="kɔnyaa_915">
    <lexical-unit><form lang="kqs"><text>kɔnyaa</text></form></lexical-unit>
    <trait name="status" value="check"/>
    <sense id="kɔnyaa_915_s1">
      <grammatical-info value="Noun"/>
      <gloss lang="fr"><text>épidémie mortelle (nàà n'kɔnyaa « peste »)</text></gloss>
      <gloss lang="en"><text>deadly epidemic (nàà n'kɔnyaa 'pestilence')</text></gloss>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="2.5.2 Disease"/>
    </sense>
    <note><form lang="fr"><text>Seulement dans nàà n'kɔnyaa « la peste » (Ex 5,3 ; Lv 26,25).</text></form></note>
  </entry>
  <entry id="kɔŋɔ_916">
    <lexical-unit><form lang="kqs"><text>kɔŋɔ</text></form></lexical-unit>
    <trait name="status" value="attested"/>
    <field type="plural"><form lang="kqs"><text>kɔŋɔla</text></form></field>
