      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="5.5 Fire"/>
    </sense>
    <field type="southern-kissi-sense"><form lang="en"><text>burn, be burning</text></form></field>
    <note type="source"><form lang="en"><text>BKG: 97 occurrences, first GEN.19.28; Keita 1979, p. 115: Lomöö; Childs 2000, p. 232: lòmɔ̀ɔ́</text></form></note>
    <note><form lang="fr"><text>lum : radical négatif selon Keita (lumnin, ISA 43,2), mais aussi « cuire » (GEN 19,3).</text></form></note>
  </entry>
  <entry id="lon_1029">
    <lexical-unit><form lang="kqs"><text>lon</text></form></lexical-unit>
    <trait name="status" value="attested"/>
    <sense id="lon_1029_s1">
      <grammatical-info value="Adverb"/>
      <gloss lang="fr"><text>là, là-bas</text></gloss>
      <gloss lang="en"><text>there</text></gloss>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="9.2.2 Adverbs"/>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="8.5.1 Here, there"/>
    </sense>
    <note type="source"><form lang="en"><text>BKG: 1422 occurrences, first GEN.2.10; Childs 2000, p. 232: lɔ́ŋ</text></form></note>
  </entry>
  <entry id="loo_1030">
    <lexical-unit><form lang="kqs"><text>loo</text></form></lexical-unit>
    <trait name="status" value="attested"/>
    <sense id="loo_1030_s1">
      <grammatical-info value="Postposition"/>
      <gloss lang="fr"><text>sans, privé de</text></gloss>
      <gloss lang="en"><text>without, lacking</text></gloss>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="9.2.4 Prepositions, postpositions"/>
    </sense>
    <note type="source"><form lang="en"><text>BKG: 573 occurrences, first GEN.14.21</text></form></note>
  </entry>
  <entry id="looku_1031">
    <lexical-unit><form lang="kqs"><text>looku</text></form></lexical-unit>
    <trait name="status" value="attested"/>
    <sense id="looku_1031_s1">
      <grammatical-info value="Verb"/>
      <gloss lang="fr"><text>s'y prendre, faire (comment) ; réussir à</text></gloss>
      <gloss lang="en"><text>manage, contrive (how)</text></gloss>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="9.1.2 Do"/>
    </sense>
    <note type="source"><form lang="en"><text>BKG: 44 occurrences, first GEN.27.20; Childs 2000, p. 233: lòòkòó</text></form></note>
    <note><form lang="fr"><text>Seule la forme courte est attestée : Vɛɛ n looku yɛ … ? « Comment as-tu fait pour … ? » (Gn 27,20).</text></form></note>
  </entry>
  <entry id="loolio_1032">
    <lexical-unit><form lang="kqs"><text>loolio</text></form></lexical-unit>
    <trait name="noun-class" value="o"/>
    <trait name="status" value="attested"/>
    <sense id="loolio_1032_s1">
      <grammatical-info value="Noun"/>
      <gloss lang="fr"><text>boue</text></gloss>
      <gloss lang="en"><text>mud</text></gloss>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="1.2.2 Substance, matter"/>
    </sense>
    <note type="source"><form lang="en"><text>BKG: 27 occurrences, first 1SA.4.12; Keita 1979, p. 155: Loolio; Childs 2000, p. 233: lòòlìóó</text></form></note>
  </entry>
  <entry id="loonanndo_1033">
    <lexical-unit><form lang="kqs"><text>loonanndo</text></form></lexical-unit>
    <trait name="status" value="attested"/>
    <variant><form lang="kqs"><text>loonan</text></form></variant>
    <variant><form lang="kqs"><text>loonannde</text></form></variant>
    <variant><form lang="kqs"><text>loonannden</text></form></variant>
    <sense id="loonanndo_1033_s1">
      <grammatical-info value="Adjective"/>
      <gloss lang="fr"><text>commémoratif ; mémorial</text></gloss>
      <gloss lang="en"><text>commemorative; memorial</text></gloss>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="3.2.6 Remember"/>
    </sense>
    <note type="source"><form lang="en"><text>BKG: 8 occurrences, first EXO.13.9</text></form></note>
    <note><form lang="fr"><text>De loonɔnndo « se souvenir ». ɲɛ loonanndo « mémorial » (Ex 13,16) ; paale loonannde « jour du souvenir » (Ex 12,41) ; Sɛbɛ loonan « livre des annales » (2 Ch 13,22).</text></form></note>
  </entry>
  <entry id="loonɔnndo_1034">
    <lexical-unit><form lang="kqs"><text>loonɔnndo</text></form></lexical-unit>
    <trait name="status" value="attested"/>
    <variant><form lang="kqs"><text>loonun</text></form></variant>
    <variant><form lang="kqs"><text>loonunnin</text></form></variant>
    <sense id="loonɔnndo_1034_s1">
      <grammatical-info value="Verb"/>
      <gloss lang="fr"><text>se souvenir</text></gloss>
      <gloss lang="en"><text>remember</text></gloss>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="3.2.6 Remember"/>
    </sense>
    <note type="source"><form lang="en"><text>BKG: 50 occurrences, first GEN.9.13; Childs 2000, p. 233: lòònɔ̀ŋndɔ́</text></form></note>
  </entry>
  <entry id="lou_1035">
    <lexical-unit><form lang="kqs"><text>lou</text></form></lexical-unit>
    <trait name="status" value="attested"/>
    <variant><form lang="kqs"><text>lonin</text></form></variant>
    <sense id="lou_1035_s1">
      <grammatical-info value="Verb"/>
      <gloss lang="fr"><text>rester, demeurer ; continuer (à), persister</text></gloss>
      <gloss lang="en"><text>remain, stay; keep on, persist</text></gloss>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="5.9 Live, stay"/>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="8.4.6 Aspectual time"/>
    </sense>
    <field type="southern-kissi-sense"><form lang="en"><text>remain, keep on; also get lost, disappear; adopt into the family</text></form></field>
    <note type="source"><form lang="en"><text>BKG: 80 occurrences, first GEN.7.3; Childs 2000, p. 233: lòó</text></form></note>
    <note><form lang="fr"><text>Radical lo : lo yoomu « rester en vie » ; à lo ndu dioo « ils continuèrent à le manger » (Ex 16,35). lou o diomnde … coo « rester fidèle à sa parole » (Gn 24,27).</text></form></note>
  </entry>
  <entry id="lovɛi_1036">
    <lexical-unit><form lang="kqs"><text>lovɛi</text></form></lexical-unit>
    <trait name="noun-class" value="i"/>
    <trait name="status" value="respelled"/>
    <sense id="lovɛi_1036_s1">
      <grammatical-info value="Noun"/>
      <gloss lang="fr"><text>hernie étranglée</text></gloss>
      <gloss lang="en"><text>strangulated hernia</text></gloss>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="2.5.2 Disease"/>
    </sense>
    <field type="southern-kissi-sense"><form lang="en"><text>hernia</text></form></field>
    <note type="source"><form lang="en"><text>Keita 1979, p. 161: Lovèi; Childs 2000, p. 233: lòwɛ̀í</text></form></note>
  </entry>
  <entry id="luakolanɔɔ_1037">
    <lexical-unit><form lang="kqs"><text>luakolanɔɔ</text></form></lexical-unit>
    <trait name="noun-class" value="o"/>
    <trait name="status" value="respelled"/>
    <sense id="luakolanɔɔ_1037_s1">
      <grammatical-info value="Noun"/>
      <gloss lang="fr"><text>tisserand</text></gloss>
      <gloss lang="en"><text>weaver</text></gloss>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="6.6.1 Working with cloth"/>
    </sense>
    <note type="source"><form lang="en"><text>Keita 1979, p. 145: Luakolanöö</text></form></note>
  </entry>
  <entry id="lueinun_1038">
    <lexical-unit><form lang="kqs"><text>lueinun</text></form></lexical-unit>
    <trait name="status" value="attested"/>
    <sense id="lueinun_1038_s1">
      <grammatical-info value="Verb"/>
      <gloss lang="fr"><text>aller vers (une femme) ; (… yoomuan) prendre courage, se fortifier</text></gloss>
      <gloss lang="en"><text>go in to (a woman); (… yoomuan) take courage, be strong</text></gloss>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="2.6.2 Sexual relations"/>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="3.4.1 Feel good"/>
    </sense>
    <note type="source"><form lang="en"><text>BKG: 16 occurrences, first GEN.6.19</text></form></note>
    <note><form lang="fr"><text>Moyen de lueiyo. lueinun … coo « aller vers (une femme) » (Gn 16,2) ; réciproque lueinan yoomuan « s'encourager mutuellement » (1 Th 5,11).</text></form></note>
  </entry>
  <entry id="lueiyo_1039">
    <lexical-unit><form lang="kqs"><text>lueiyo</text></form></lexical-unit>
    <trait name="status" value="attested"/>
    <variant><form lang="kqs"><text>luei</text></form></variant>
    <variant><form lang="kqs"><text>lueinin</text></form></variant>
    <sense id="lueiyo_1039_s1">
      <grammatical-info value="Verb"/>
      <gloss lang="fr"><text>faire entrer, introduire, mettre dans ; causer (un malheur)</text></gloss>
      <gloss lang="en"><text>bring in, put in; cause (grief)</text></gloss>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="7.3.2 Move something in a direction"/>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="7.3.3 Take somewhere"/>
    </sense>
    <field type="southern-kissi-sense"><form lang="en"><text>put in; also carry back, put away, return</text></form></field>
    <note type="source"><form lang="en"><text>BKG: 114 occurrences, first GEN.6.5; Childs 2000, p. 236: lùèìyó</text></form></note>
    <note><form lang="fr"><text>Causatif de luɛyɔɔ « entrer ». luei … mɔnɛi lueiyo « causer du chagrin » (Gn 26,35). Bénéfactif lueilul « rapporter (un profit) à » (Pr 3,14).</text></form></note>
  </entry>
  <entry id="lum_1040">
    <lexical-unit><form lang="kqs"><text>lum</text></form></lexical-unit>
    <trait name="status" value="attested"/>
    <sense id="lum_1040_s1">
      <grammatical-info value="Verb"/>
      <gloss lang="fr"><text>cuire (au four), préparer (un repas)</text></gloss>
      <gloss lang="en"><text>bake, prepare (a meal)</text></gloss>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="5.2.1 Food preparation"/>
    </sense>
    <note type="source"><form lang="en"><text>BKG: 13 occurrences, first GEN.19.3</text></form></note>
  </entry>
  <entry id="lusullo_1041">
    <lexical-unit><form lang="kqs"><text>lusullo</text></form></lexical-unit>
    <trait name="status" value="attested"/>
    <variant><form lang="kqs"><text>lusul</text></form></variant>
    <variant><form lang="kqs"><text>lusulaa</text></form></variant>
    <sense id="lusullo_1041_s1">
      <grammatical-info value="Verb"/>
      <gloss lang="fr"><text>être lourd ; poids</text></gloss>
      <gloss lang="en"><text>be heavy; weight</text></gloss>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="8.2.8 Measure"/>
    </sense>
    <note type="source"><form lang="en"><text>BKG: 17 occurrences, first EXO.14.25</text></form></note>
  </entry>
  <entry id="luusian_1042">
    <lexical-unit><form lang="kqs"><text>luusian</text></form></lexical-unit>
    <trait name="status" value="attested"/>
    <sense id="luusian_1042_s1">
      <grammatical-info value="Verb"/>
      <gloss lang="fr"><text>errer, s'égarer ; être perdu</text></gloss>
      <gloss lang="en"><text>wander, go astray; be lost</text></gloss>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="7.2.1 Manner of movement"/>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="7.6.3 Lose, misplace"/>
    </sense>
    <field type="southern-kissi-sense"><form lang="en"><text>play tricks, act foolishly; get lost, go missing</text></form></field>
    <note type="source"><form lang="en"><text>BKG: 16 occurrences, first GEN.21.14; Childs 2000, p. 237: lùùsìá</text></form></note>
  </entry>
  <entry id="luŋ_1043">
    <lexical-unit><form lang="kqs"><text>luŋ</text></form></lexical-unit>
    <trait name="status" value="attested"/>
    <sense id="luŋ_1043_s1">
      <grammatical-info value="Noun"/>
      <gloss lang="fr"><text>place publique ; (o luŋ) en public, dehors</text></gloss>
      <gloss lang="en"><text>public square; (o luŋ) in public, outside</text></gloss>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="8.5.4 Area"/>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="6.5.4 Infrastructure"/>
    </sense>
    <note type="source"><form lang="en"><text>BKG: 5 occurrences, first EXO.4.10</text></form></note>
    <note><form lang="fr"><text>cal o luŋ « s'asseoir sur la place » (Jg 19,15) ; yonda … o luŋ kpendekele « proclamer en public » (Lc 12,3).</text></form></note>
  </entry>
  <entry id="luɛyaa_1044">
    <lexical-unit><form lang="kqs"><text>luɛyaa</text></form></lexical-unit>
    <trait name="status" value="attested"/>
    <field type="plural"><form lang="kqs"><text>luɛyaalan</text></form></field>
    <variant><form lang="kqs"><text>luɛyaala</text></form></variant>
    <sense id="luɛyaa_1044_s1">
      <grammatical-info value="Noun"/>
      <gloss lang="fr"><text>entrée, porte (de ville)</text></gloss>
      <gloss lang="en"><text>entrance, gate</text></gloss>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="6.5.2 Parts of a building"/>
    </sense>
    <note type="source"><form lang="en"><text>BKG: 85 occurrences, first EXO.4.25</text></form></note>
    <note><form lang="fr"><text>Nom verbal de luɛyɔɔ « entrer ».</text></form></note>
  </entry>
  <entry id="luɛyɔɔ_1045">
    <lexical-unit><form lang="kqs"><text>luɛyɔɔ</text></form></lexical-unit>
    <trait name="status" value="attested"/>
    <variant><form lang="kqs"><text>luɛi</text></form></variant>
    <variant><form lang="kqs"><text>luɛinin</text></form></variant>
    <sense id="luɛyɔɔ_1045_s1">
      <grammatical-info value="Verb"/>
      <gloss lang="fr"><text>entrer ; arriver, survenir</text></gloss>
      <gloss lang="en"><text>enter, go in; come, arrive</text></gloss>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="7.2.3 Move toward something"/>
    </sense>
    <field type="southern-kissi-sense"><form lang="en"><text>enter, come in; put in; produce in quantity (crops)</text></form></field>
    <note type="source"><form lang="en"><text>BKG: 209 occurrences, first GEN.6.18; Childs 2000, p. 236: lùèyɔ̀ɔ́</text></form></note>
  </entry>
  <entry id="luɛyɔɔninndo_1046">
    <lexical-unit><form lang="kqs"><text>luɛyɔɔninndo</text></form></lexical-unit>
    <trait name="noun-class" value="o"/>
    <trait name="status" value="attested"/>
    <sense id="luɛyɔɔninndo_1046_s1">
      <grammatical-info value="Noun"/>
      <gloss lang="fr"><text>pot-de-vin</text></gloss>
      <gloss lang="en"><text>bribe</text></gloss>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="6.8.4 Financial transaction"/>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="4.7 Law"/>
    </sense>
    <note type="source"><form lang="en"><text>BKG: 14 occurrences, first DEU.27.25</text></form></note>
    <note><form lang="fr"><text>De luɛyɔɔ « entrer ». cɛl luɛyɔɔninndo « accepter un pot-de-vin » (Dt 27,25).</text></form></note>
  </entry>
  <entry id="lɔaa_1047">
    <lexical-unit><form lang="kqs"><text>lɔaa</text></form></lexical-unit>
    <trait name="status" value="attested"/>
    <variant><form lang="kqs"><text>lɔanin</text></form></variant>
    <variant><form lang="kqs"><text>lɔa</text></form></variant>
    <sense id="lɔaa_1047_s1">
      <grammatical-info value="Verb"/>
      <gloss lang="fr"><text>frapper ; jouer (d'un instrument) ; frapper (à la porte)</text></gloss>
      <gloss lang="en"><text>strike, beat; play (an instrument) ; strike, beat; play (an instrument); knock</text></gloss>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="7.7.1 Hit"/>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="4.2.3 Music"/>
    </sense>
    <field type="southern-kissi-sense"><form lang="en"><text>hit, beat, strike</text></form></field>
    <note type="source"><form lang="en"><text>BKG: 105 occurrences, first GEN.4.21; Keita 1979, p. 115: Löö; Childs 2000, p. 235: lɔ̀wàá</text></form></note>
    <note><form lang="fr"><text>Keita écrit löö (radicaux lö, loo, löa) ; la Bible a lɔaa (GEN 32,26 ; GEN 4,21) et lɔanin (ISA 11,4).</text></form></note>
  </entry>
  <entry id="lɔalaa_1048">
    <lexical-unit><form lang="kqs"><text>lɔalaa</text></form></lexical-unit>
    <trait name="status" value="attested"/>
    <variant><form lang="kqs"><text>lɔalu</text></form></variant>
    <variant><form lang="kqs"><text>lɔalunin</text></form></variant>
    <sense id="lɔalaa_1048_s1">
      <grammatical-info value="Verb"/>
      <gloss lang="fr"><text>accuser, dénoncer, calomnier</text></gloss>
      <gloss lang="en"><text>accuse, denounce, slander</text></gloss>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="4.7.5 Trial"/>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="3.5.1 Say"/>
    </sense>
    <note type="source"><form lang="en"><text>BKG: 1 occurrences, first ZEC.3.1</text></form></note>
    <note><form lang="fr"><text>vana lɔalaa n'vanndo « l'accusateur » (Za 3,1).</text></form></note>
  </entry>
  <entry id="lɔan_1049">
    <lexical-unit><form lang="kqs"><text>lɔan</text></form></lexical-unit>
    <trait name="noun-class" value="an"/>
    <trait name="status" value="attested"/>
    <variant><form lang="kqs"><text>lɔma</text></form></variant>
    <sense id="lɔan_1049_s1">
      <grammatical-info value="Noun"/>
      <gloss lang="fr"><text>sommeil</text></gloss>
      <gloss lang="en"><text>sleep</text></gloss>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="5.7 Sleep"/>
    </sense>
    <field type="southern-kissi-sense"><form lang="en"><text>sleep (verb)</text></form></field>
    <note type="source"><form lang="en"><text>BKG: 123 occurrences, first GEN.2.21; Childs 2000, p. 235: lùáŋ</text></form></note>
  </entry>
  <entry id="lɔl_1050">
    <lexical-unit><form lang="kqs"><text>lɔl</text></form></lexical-unit>
    <trait name="status" value="attested"/>
    <sense id="lɔl_1050_s1">
      <grammatical-info value="Verb"/>
      <gloss lang="fr"><text>passer la nuit, loger, séjourner</text></gloss>
      <gloss lang="en"><text>spend the night, lodge, dwell</text></gloss>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="5.9 Live, stay"/>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="5.7 Sleep"/>
    </sense>
    <note type="source"><form lang="en"><text>BKG: 81 occurrences, first GEN.4.20</text></form></note>
    <note><form lang="fr"><text>Forme longue non attestée dans la Bible.</text></form></note>
  </entry>
  <entry id="lɔloo_1051">
    <lexical-unit><form lang="kqs"><text>lɔloo</text></form></lexical-unit>
    <trait name="noun-class" value="o"/>
    <trait name="status" value="attested"/>
    <field type="plural"><form lang="kqs"><text>lɔlulan</text></form></field>
    <variant><form lang="kqs"><text>lɔlu</text></form></variant>
    <sense id="lɔloo_1051_s1">
      <grammatical-info value="Noun"/>
      <gloss lang="fr"><text>cuisse</text></gloss>
      <gloss lang="en"><text>thigh</text></gloss>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="2.1.3 Limb"/>
    </sense>
    <note type="source"><form lang="en"><text>BKG: 5 occurrences, first GEN.32.32; Keita 1979, p. 132: Löluoo; Childs 2000, p. 234: lɔ̀lòó</text></form></note>
  </entry>
  <entry id="lɔlu_1052">
    <lexical-unit><form lang="kqs"><text>lɔlu</text></form></lexical-unit>
    <trait name="status" value="attested"/>
    <sense id="lɔlu_1052_s1">
      <grammatical-info value="Noun"/>
      <gloss lang="fr"><text>cuisse</text></gloss>
      <gloss lang="en"><text>thigh</text></gloss>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="2.1.3 Limb"/>
    </sense>
    <note type="source"><form lang="en"><text>BKG: 25 occurrences, first GEN.24.2; Childs 2000, p. 234: lɔ̀lɔ̀ɔ́</text></form></note>
  </entry>
  <entry id="lɔluan_1053">
    <lexical-unit><form lang="kqs"><text>lɔluan</text></form></lexical-unit>
    <trait name="noun-class" value="an"/>
    <trait name="status" value="attested"/>
    <sense id="lɔluan_1053_s1">
      <grammatical-info value="Noun"/>
      <gloss lang="fr"><text>salive, crachat</text></gloss>
      <gloss lang="en"><text>saliva, spittle</text></gloss>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="2.2.3 Spit, saliva"/>
    </sense>
    <note type="source"><form lang="en"><text>BKG: 14 occurrences, first LEV.15.8; Keita 1979, p. 132: Löluan; Childs 2000, p. 234: lɔ̀lùáŋ</text></form></note>
  </entry>
  <entry id="lɔ́ngùlɔn_1054">
    <lexical-unit><form lang="kqs"><text>lɔ́ngùlɔn</text></form></lexical-unit>
    <trait name="status" value="attested"/>
    <sense id="lɔ́ngùlɔn_1054_s1">
      <grammatical-info value="Ideophone"/>
      <gloss lang="fr"><text>sans force, inerte ; (sommeil) profond</text></gloss>
      <gloss lang="en"><text>limp, powerless; (sleep) deep</text></gloss>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="2.4.2 Weak"/>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="9.2.8 Ideophones"/>
    </sense>
    <note type="source"><form lang="en"><text>BKG: 5 occurrences, first GEN.15.12</text></form></note>
    <note><form lang="fr"><text>diallon vu Abram lɔ́ngùlɔn « Abram fut saisi d'une torpeur » (Gn 15,12) ; bala … vi lɔ́ngùlɔn « les bras tomberont sans force » (Ez 30,25).</text></form></note>
  </entry>
  <entry id="lɔngɔlian_1055">
    <lexical-unit><form lang="kqs"><text>lɔngɔlian</text></form></lexical-unit>
    <trait name="status" value="attested"/>
    <variant><form lang="kqs"><text>lɔngɔlianndo</text></form></variant>
    <sense id="lɔngɔlian_1055_s1">
      <grammatical-info value="Verb"/>
      <gloss lang="fr"><text>se rouler, se vautrer ; être souillé</text></gloss>
      <gloss lang="en"><text>roll, wallow; be defiled</text></gloss>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="7.2.1 Manner of movement"/>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="5.6.1 Clean, dirty"/>
    </sense>
    <note type="source"><form lang="en"><text>BKG: 8 occurrences, first DEU.32.5</text></form></note>
    <note><form lang="fr"><text>lɔngɔlianndo o kooma nɔmndan nin « te débattant dans ton sang » (Ez 16,6). Causatif lɔngɔliaa « fouler dans la boue » (Is 26,5).</text></form></note>
  </entry>
  <entry id="lɔu_1056">
    <lexical-unit><form lang="kqs"><text>lɔu</text></form></lexical-unit>
    <trait name="status" value="attested"/>
    <variant><form lang="kqs"><text>lɔa</text></form></variant>
    <sense id="lɔu_1056_s1">
      <grammatical-info value="Verb"/>
      <gloss lang="fr"><text>tresser, tisser, filer ; mouler (briques)</text></gloss>
      <gloss lang="en"><text>braid, weave, spin; mould (bricks)</text></gloss>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="6.6.1 Working with cloth"/>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="6.6.4 Crafts"/>
    </sense>
    <field type="southern-kissi-sense"><form lang="en"><text>plait, braid (baskets, slings)</text></form></field>
    <note type="source"><form lang="en"><text>BKG: 19 occurrences, first EXO.1.14; Keita 1979, p. 110: Löw; Childs 2000, p. 235: lɔ̀ɔ́</text></form></note>
    <note><form lang="fr"><text>Keita écrit löw ; la Bible écrit lɔu : yiiŋii lɔu « filer le poil de chèvre » (EXO 35,26), lɔa kambɛiyo « tresser une corbeille » (EXO 2,3), kpilikion lɔu « faire des briques » (EXO 5,7).</text></form></note>
  </entry>
  <entry id="lɔwviaa_1057">
    <lexical-unit><form lang="kqs"><text>lɔwviaa</text></form></lexical-unit>
    <trait name="status" value="attested"/>
    <sense id="lɔwviaa_1057_s1">
      <grammatical-info value="Verb"/>
      <gloss lang="fr"><text>mordre</text></gloss>
      <gloss lang="en"><text>bite</text></gloss>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="1.6.4 Animal actions"/>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="5.2.2 Eat"/>
    </sense>
    <note type="source"><form lang="en"><text>BKG: 19 occurrences, first NUM.21.6</text></form></note>
  </entry>
  <entry id="lɔ́ɔ́_1058">
    <lexical-unit><form lang="kqs"><text>lɔ́ɔ́</text></form></lexical-unit>
    <trait name="noun-class" value="o"/>
    <trait name="status" value="attested"/>
    <field type="plural"><form lang="kqs"><text>lɔ́ɔ́lan</text></form></field>
    <sense id="lɔ́ɔ́_1058_s1">
      <grammatical-info value="Noun"/>
      <gloss lang="fr"><text>semaine ; marché</text></gloss>
      <gloss lang="en"><text>week ; market; week</text></gloss>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="8.4.1 Period of time"/>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="6.9.4 Commerce"/>
    </sense>
    <note type="source"><form lang="en"><text>BKG: 1717 occurrences, first GEN.3.19; Keita 1979, p. 152: Löö; Childs 2000, p. 235: lɔ́ɔ́</text></form></note>
    <note><form lang="fr"><text>Homonyme de lɔ́ɔ́ « jusqu'à ». La Bible a le pluriel lɔ́ɔ́lan « semaines » (Lv 23,15) ; Childs donne « marché, semaine ». Pour la place du marché, la Bible dit luŋ (Mt 11,16). Ne pas confondre avec la conjonction lɔ́ɔ́.</text></form></note>
  </entry>
  <entry id="lɔɔmei_1059">
    <lexical-unit><form lang="kqs"><text>lɔɔmei</text></form></lexical-unit>
    <trait name="noun-class" value="i"/>
    <trait name="status" value="respelled"/>
    <sense id="lɔɔmei_1059_s1">
      <grammatical-info value="Noun"/>
      <gloss lang="fr"><text>morve</text></gloss>
      <gloss lang="en"><text>nasal mucus</text></gloss>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="2.2.4 Mucus"/>
    </sense>
    <note type="source"><form lang="en"><text>Keita 1979, p. 132: Löömei; Childs 2000, p. 235: lɔ̀ɔ̀mèí</text></form></note>
  </entry>
  <entry id="lɔɔnɔnndo_1060">
    <lexical-unit><form lang="kqs"><text>lɔɔnɔnndo</text></form></lexical-unit>
    <trait name="status" value="attested"/>
    <sense id="lɔɔnɔnndo_1060_s1">
      <grammatical-info value="Verb"/>
      <gloss lang="fr"><text>se frapper</text></gloss>
      <gloss lang="en"><text>beat oneself</text></gloss>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="7.7.1 Hit"/>
    </sense>
    <note type="source"><form lang="en"><text>BKG: 4 occurrences, first ISA.51.22; Keita 1979, p. 115: Löönönndo</text></form></note>
    <note><form lang="fr"><text>Moyen de lɔaa : buŋnde lɔɔnɔnndo « se frapper la poitrine » (LUK 18,13).</text></form></note>
  </entry>
  <entry id="lɛ_1061">
    <lexical-unit><form lang="kqs"><text>lɛ</text></form></lexical-unit>
    <trait name="status" value="attested"/>
    <sense id="lɛ_1061_s1">
      <grammatical-info value="Adverb"/>
      <gloss lang="fr"><text>encore ; (avec négation) ne … plus</text></gloss>
      <gloss lang="en"><text>still; (with negation) no longer, any more</text></gloss>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="9.2.2 Adverbs"/>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="8.4.6 Aspectual time"/>
    </sense>
    <note type="source"><form lang="en"><text>BKG: 775 occurrences, first GEN.4.14</text></form></note>
    <note><form lang="fr"><text>poonpoondo muungu lɛ ndu o ibuŋ te « la colombe ne revint plus vers lui » (Gn 8,12).</text></form></note>
  </entry>
  <entry id="lɛan_1062">
    <lexical-unit><form lang="kqs"><text>lɛan</text></form></lexical-unit>
    <trait name="noun-class" value="an"/>
    <trait name="status" value="attested"/>
    <sense id="lɛan_1062_s1">
      <grammatical-info value="Noun"/>
      <gloss lang="fr"><text>miel</text></gloss>
      <gloss lang="en"><text>honey</text></gloss>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="5.2.3 Types of food"/>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="6.4.4 Beekeeping"/>
    </sense>
    <note type="source"><form lang="en"><text>BKG: 27 occurrences, first GEN.43.11; Keita 1979, p. 136: Lian; Childs 2000, p. 230: lìáŋ</text></form></note>
    <note><form lang="fr"><text>Keita écrit Lian ; la Bible écrit lɛan.</text></form></note>
  </entry>
  <entry id="lɛfɔɔ_1063">
    <lexical-unit><form lang="kqs"><text>lɛfɔɔ</text></form></lexical-unit>
    <trait name="noun-class" value="o"/>
    <trait name="status" value="respelled"/>
    <variant><form lang="kqs"><text>lɛfɛ</text></form></variant>
    <sense id="lɛfɔɔ_1063_s1">
      <grammatical-info value="Noun"/>
      <gloss lang="fr"><text>drapeau, étendard</text></gloss>
      <gloss lang="en"><text>flag, banner</text></gloss>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="3.5.6 Sign, symbol"/>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="4.8.3 War"/>
    </sense>
    <field type="southern-kissi-sense"><form lang="en"><text>flag; also a wind-blown bamboo noisemaker that scares birds</text></form></field>
    <note type="source"><form lang="en"><text>Keita 1979, p. 159: Lèföö; Childs 2000, p. 229: lɛ̀fɔ̀ɔ́</text></form></note>
    <note><form lang="fr"><text>Forme radicale lɛfɛ « étendard » dans la Bible (Ex 17,15 ; Nb 2,2), comme dɛ̀ndɛ̀ pour dɛ̀ndɔ̀ɔ́.</text></form></note>
  </entry>
  <entry id="lɛlɔn_1064">
    <lexical-unit><form lang="kqs"><text>lɛlɔn</text></form></lexical-unit>
    <trait name="status" value="respelled"/>
    <sense id="lɛlɔn_1064_s1">
      <grammatical-info value="Noun"/>
      <gloss lang="fr"><text>lèpre</text></gloss>
      <gloss lang="en"><text>leprosy</text></gloss>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="2.5.2 Disease"/>
    </sense>
    <note type="source"><form lang="en"><text>Keita 1979, p. 161: Lèlön; Childs 2000, p. 229: lɛ̀lɔ̌ŋ</text></form></note>
  </entry>
  <entry id="lɛmbɛvilɛiyo_1065">
    <lexical-unit><form lang="kqs"><text>lɛmbɛvilɛiyo</text></form></lexical-unit>
    <trait name="noun-class" value="o"/>
    <trait name="status" value="check"/>
    <sense id="lɛmbɛvilɛiyo_1065_s1">
      <grammatical-info value="Noun"/>
      <gloss lang="fr"><text>pantalon</text></gloss>
      <gloss lang="en"><text>trousers</text></gloss>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="5.3 Clothing"/>
    </sense>
    <note type="source"><form lang="en"><text>Keita 1979, p. 144: Lèmbèvilèiyo; Childs 2000, p. 229: lɛ̀mbɔ̀ɔ́</text></form></note>
    <note><form lang="fr"><text>Childs : lɛ̀mbɔ̀ɔ́, pl. lɛ̀mbɛ̀láŋ « pantalon ». La Bible a lɛmbɛla lebɛngulan « caleçons » (Ex 28,42) ; lɛmbɛ-vílɛ́i (Dt 7,14) y signifie « stérile ».</text></form></note>
  </entry>
  <entry id="lɛu_1066">
    <lexical-unit><form lang="kqs"><text>lɛu</text></form></lexical-unit>
    <trait name="noun-class" value="o"/>
    <trait name="status" value="respelled"/>
    <field type="plural"><form lang="kqs"><text>lɛa</text></form></field>
    <sense id="lɛu_1066_s1">
      <grammatical-info value="Noun"/>
      <gloss lang="fr"><text>abeille</text></gloss>
      <gloss lang="en"><text>bee</text></gloss>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="1.6.1 Types of animals"/>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="6.4.4 Beekeeping"/>
    </sense>
    <note type="source"><form lang="en"><text>Keita 1979, p. 136: Lèu</text></form></note>
    <note><form lang="fr"><text>Le singulier n'est pas dans la Bible ; le pluriel lɛa « abeilles » y est (DEU.1.44, JDG.14.8).</text></form></note>
  </entry>
  <entry id="lɛvɛnndo_1067">
    <lexical-unit><form lang="kqs"><text>lɛvɛnndo</text></form></lexical-unit>
    <trait name="status" value="attested"/>
    <variant><form lang="kqs"><text>lɛvɛn</text></form></variant>
    <sense id="lɛvɛnndo_1067_s1">
      <grammatical-info value="Noun"/>
      <gloss lang="fr"><text>levain</text></gloss>
      <gloss lang="en"><text>leaven, yeast</text></gloss>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="5.2.1 Food preparation"/>
    </sense>
    <note type="source"><form lang="en"><text>BKG: 31 occurrences, first EXO.12.15</text></form></note>
    <note><form lang="fr"><text>bulu toosian a lɛvɛn too « pain sans levain ».</text></form></note>
  </entry>
  <entry id="lɛwve_1068">
    <lexical-unit><form lang="kqs"><text>lɛwve</text></form></lexical-unit>
    <trait name="noun-class" value="i"/>
    <trait name="status" value="attested"/>
    <field type="plural"><form lang="kqs"><text>lɛwvon</text></form></field>
    <variant><form lang="kqs"><text>lɛvii</text></form></variant>
    <variant><form lang="kqs"><text>lɛvun</text></form></variant>
    <variant><form lang="kqs"><text>lɛvi</text></form></variant>
    <sense id="lɛwve_1068_s1">
      <grammatical-info value="Noun"/>
      <gloss lang="fr"><text>branche d'arbre</text></gloss>
      <gloss lang="en"><text>branch</text></gloss>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="1.5.5 Parts of a plant"/>
    </sense>
    <note type="source"><form lang="en"><text>BKG: 4 occurrences, first GEN.49.11; Keita 1979, p. 139: Lèwve; Childs 2000, p. 230: lèùwé</text></form></note>
  </entry>
  <entry id="lɛŋnden_1069">
    <lexical-unit><form lang="kqs"><text>lɛŋnden</text></form></lexical-unit>
    <trait name="noun-class" value="len"/>
    <trait name="status" value="attested"/>
    <field type="plural"><form lang="kqs"><text>lɛŋii</text></form></field>
    <variant><form lang="kqs"><text>lɛŋnde</text></form></variant>
    <sense id="lɛŋnden_1069_s1">
      <grammatical-info value="Noun"/>
      <gloss lang="fr"><text>pays, nation ; terre</text></gloss>
      <gloss lang="en"><text>country, nation; land, earth</text></gloss>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="4.6.7 Region"/>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="1.2 World"/>
    </sense>
    <field type="southern-kissi-sense"><form lang="en"><text>land, ground, area; country of origin; world, earth; floor</text></form></field>
    <note type="source"><form lang="en"><text>BKG: 1286 occurrences, first GEN.1; Keita 1979, p. 155: Lènnden; Childs 2000, p. 229: lɛ̀ŋndéŋ</text></form></note>
    <note><form lang="fr"><text>Keita écrit Lènnden ; la Bible lɛŋnden.</text></form></note>
  </entry>
  <entry id="lɛɛlɛ_1070">
    <lexical-unit><form lang="kqs"><text>lɛɛlɛ</text></form></lexical-unit>
    <trait name="status" value="attested"/>
    <sense id="lɛɛlɛ_1070_s1">
      <grammatical-info value="Noun"/>
      <gloss lang="fr"><text>heure</text></gloss>
      <gloss lang="en"><text>hour</text></gloss>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="8.4.4 Telling time"/>
    </sense>
    <note type="source"><form lang="en"><text>BKG: 19 occurrences, first MAT.20.3</text></form></note>
  </entry>
  <entry id="lɛɛndei_1071">
    <lexical-unit><form lang="kqs"><text>lɛɛndei</text></form></lexical-unit>
    <trait name="noun-class" value="i"/>
    <trait name="status" value="attested"/>
    <field type="plural"><form lang="kqs"><text>lɛɛndun</text></form></field>
    <sense id="lɛɛndei_1071_s1">
      <grammatical-info value="Noun"/>
      <gloss lang="fr"><text>rameau, jeune branche</text></gloss>
      <gloss lang="en"><text>twig, bough</text></gloss>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="1.5.5 Parts of a plant"/>
    </sense>
    <note type="source"><form lang="en"><text>BKG: 1 occurrences, first EZK.17.22</text></form></note>
    <note><form lang="fr"><text>Pluriel : lɛɛndun ndɔn « ses rameaux » (Ps 80,12).</text></form></note>
  </entry>
  <entry id="lɛɛndo_1072">
    <lexical-unit><form lang="kqs"><text>lɛɛndo</text></form></lexical-unit>
    <trait name="noun-class" value="o"/>
    <trait name="status" value="attested"/>
    <sense id="lɛɛndo_1072_s1">
      <grammatical-info value="Noun"/>
      <gloss lang="fr"><text>coupe-coupe, machette</text></gloss>
      <gloss lang="en"><text>machete, cutlass</text></gloss>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="6.7.1 Cutting tool"/>
    </sense>
    <note type="source"><form lang="en"><text>BKG: 2 occurrences, first ISA.10.34; Keita 1979, p. 159: Lèèndo; Childs 2000, p. 228: lɛ́ɛ́ŋndó</text></form></note>
  </entry>
  <entry id="lɛ́ɛ́siɛn_1073">
    <lexical-unit><form lang="kqs"><text>lɛ́ɛ́siɛn</text></form></lexical-unit>
    <trait name="status" value="attested"/>
    <sense id="lɛ́ɛ́siɛn_1073_s1">
      <grammatical-info value="Ideophone"/>
      <gloss lang="fr"><text>étendu sans vie</text></gloss>
      <gloss lang="en"><text>lying lifeless</text></gloss>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="2.6.6 Die"/>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="9.2.8 Ideophones"/>
    </sense>
    <note type="source"><form lang="en"><text>BKG: 11 occurrences, first 1SA.17.52</text></form></note>
    <note><form lang="fr"><text>ihini lɛ́ɛ́siɛn « gisant morts » (1 S 17,52).</text></form></note>
  </entry>
  <entry id="maa_1074">
    <lexical-unit><form lang="kqs"><text>maa</text></form></lexical-unit>
    <trait name="status" value="attested"/>
    <sense id="maa_1074_s1">
      <grammatical-info value="Connective"/>
      <gloss lang="fr"><text>que (complétive)</text></gloss>
      <gloss lang="en"><text>that (complementizer)</text></gloss>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="9.2.5 Conjunctions"/>
    </sense>
    <field type="southern-kissi-sense"><form lang="en"><text>also 'as'</text></form></field>
    <note type="source"><form lang="en"><text>BKG: 5511 occurrences, first GEN.1.4; Childs 2000, p. 238: màà</text></form></note>
  </entry>
  <entry id="maalianndo_1075">
    <lexical-unit><form lang="kqs"><text>maalianndo</text></form></lexical-unit>
    <trait name="status" value="attested"/>
    <variant><form lang="kqs"><text>maalian</text></form></variant>
    <sense id="maalianndo_1075_s1">
      <grammatical-info value="Verb"/>
      <gloss lang="fr"><text>s'entraider</text></gloss>
      <gloss lang="en"><text>help one another</text></gloss>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="4.3.4 Do good to"/>
    </sense>
    <note type="source"><form lang="en"><text>BKG: 2 occurrences, first ISA.41.6; Keita 1979, p. 110: Maalianndo</text></form></note>
    <note><form lang="fr"><text>Réciproque de malaa.</text></form></note>
  </entry>
  <entry id="maalon_1076">
    <lexical-unit><form lang="kqs"><text>maalon</text></form></lexical-unit>
    <trait name="status" value="attested"/>
    <sense id="maalon_1076_s1">
      <grammatical-info value="Noun"/>
      <gloss lang="fr"><text>riz ; blé</text></gloss>
      <gloss lang="en"><text>rice; wheat</text></gloss>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="5.2.3 Types of food"/>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="6.2.1 Growing crops"/>
    </sense>
    <note type="source"><form lang="en"><text>BKG: 76 occurrences, first GEN.30.14; Keita 1979, p. 139: Maalon</text></form></note>
    <note><form lang="fr"><text>La Bible l'emploie aussi pour le blé (GEN.30.14).</text></form></note>
  </entry>
  <entry id="máándo_1077">
    <lexical-unit><form lang="kqs"><text>máándo</text></form></lexical-unit>
    <trait name="noun-class" value="o"/>
    <trait name="status" value="attested"/>
    <variant><form lang="kqs"><text>máánnda</text></form></variant>
    <variant><form lang="kqs"><text>máánndan</text></form></variant>
    <sense id="máándo_1077_s1">
      <grammatical-info value="Noun"/>
      <gloss lang="fr"><text>sanctuaire, lieu de culte</text></gloss>
      <gloss lang="en"><text>shrine, place of worship</text></gloss>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="4.9.8 Religious things"/>
    </sense>
    <field type="southern-kissi-sense"><form lang="en"><text>place of worship; secret meeting place of the men in the forest</text></form></field>
    <note type="source"><form lang="en"><text>BKG: 7 occurrences, first JDG.17.5; Keita 1979, p. 142: Maando; Childs 2000, p. 239: máàŋndó</text></form></note>
    <note><form lang="fr"><text>Bible : cɛi máándo « maison des idoles, sanctuaire ».</text></form></note>
  </entry>
  <entry id="macɛlu_1078">
    <lexical-unit><form lang="kqs"><text>macɛlu</text></form></lexical-unit>
    <trait name="status" value="attested"/>
    <sense id="macɛlu_1078_s1">
      <grammatical-info value="Adverb"/>
      <gloss lang="fr"><text>loin, au loin</text></gloss>
      <gloss lang="en"><text>far, far away</text></gloss>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="8.2.6 Distance"/>
    </sense>
    <note type="source"><form lang="en"><text>BKG: 40 occurrences, first GEN.19.20</text></form></note>
  </entry>
  <entry id="makoo_1079">
    <lexical-unit><form lang="kqs"><text>makoo</text></form></lexical-unit>
    <trait name="noun-class" value="o"/>
    <trait name="status" value="attested"/>
    <sense id="makoo_1079_s1">
      <grammatical-info value="Noun"/>
      <gloss lang="fr"><text>besoin ; affaire</text></gloss>
      <gloss lang="en"><text>need; matter, affair</text></gloss>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="3.3 Want"/>
    </sense>
    <note type="source"><form lang="en"><text>BKG: 43 occurrences, first GEN.42.33; Keita 1979, p. 148: Makoo</text></form></note>
    <note><form lang="fr"><text>Keita : « l'affaire ». Dans la Bible, nɔ makoo a … « avoir besoin de … » (Lv 25,44 ; Lc 5,31).</text></form></note>
