      <grammatical-info value="Verb"/>
      <gloss lang="fr"><text>rouler (une pierre) ; se rouler, s'écrouler</text></gloss>
      <gloss lang="en"><text>roll (a stone); roll over, collapse</text></gloss>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="7.3.2 Move something in a direction"/>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="7.2.1 Manner of movement"/>
    </sense>
    <note type="source"><form lang="en"><text>BKG: 3 occurrences, first JDG.7.13; Childs 2000, p. 302: pìmbùlló</text></form></note>
    <note><form lang="fr"><text>La pimbul powta bɛndulan « roulez de grosses pierres » (Jos 10,18) ; mó va pimbullo « il se roulait (par terre) » (Mc 9,20).</text></form></note>
  </entry>
  <entry id="pindo_1292">
    <lexical-unit><form lang="kqs"><text>pindo</text></form></lexical-unit>
    <trait name="status" value="attested"/>
    <sense id="pindo_1292_s1">
      <grammatical-info value="Noun"/>
      <gloss lang="fr"><text>pourtour ; (… pindo) autour de</text></gloss>
      <gloss lang="en"><text>surroundings; (… pindo) around</text></gloss>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="8.6.6 Edge"/>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="9.2.4 Prepositions, postpositions"/>
    </sense>
    <note type="source"><form lang="en"><text>BKG: 97 occurrences, first GEN.19.4</text></form></note>
  </entry>
  <entry id="piondɔɔ_1293">
    <lexical-unit><form lang="kqs"><text>piondɔɔ</text></form></lexical-unit>
    <trait name="status" value="attested"/>
    <variant><form lang="kqs"><text>piondu</text></form></variant>
    <variant><form lang="kqs"><text>pendu</text></form></variant>
    <sense id="piondɔɔ_1293_s1">
      <grammatical-info value="Verb"/>
      <gloss lang="fr"><text>acheter, acquérir</text></gloss>
      <gloss lang="en"><text>buy, acquire</text></gloss>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="6.8.4 Financial transaction"/>
    </sense>
    <field type="southern-kissi-sense"><form lang="en"><text>buy, barter, exchange; pendu is one of its stems</text></form></field>
    <note type="source"><form lang="en"><text>BKG: 48 occurrences, first GEN.17.12; Childs 2000, p. 303: pìòndɔ̀ɔ́</text></form></note>
    <note><form lang="fr"><text>pendu : autre radical, au même sens (vana pendu ndu-o « celui qui l'a acheté », Lv 25,30).</text></form></note>
  </entry>
  <entry id="piow_1294">
    <lexical-unit><form lang="kqs"><text>piow</text></form></lexical-unit>
    <trait name="status" value="attested"/>
    <variant><form lang="kqs"><text>piawnin</text></form></variant>
    <sense id="piow_1294_s1">
      <grammatical-info value="Verb"/>
      <gloss lang="fr"><text>abandonner, déserter, quitter (un lieu)</text></gloss>
      <gloss lang="en"><text>abandon, desert, leave (a place)</text></gloss>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="7.2.3 Move toward something"/>
    </sense>
    <field type="southern-kissi-sense"><form lang="en"><text>make leave, drive away; also spend the evening</text></form></field>
    <note type="source"><form lang="en"><text>BKG: 12 occurrences, first ISA.27.10; Childs 2000, p. 305: pìùwó</text></form></note>
    <note><form lang="fr"><text>Yowva coocoo a visia yondoa piow lon « oiseaux et bêtes ont fui » (Jr 9,9) ; mɛɛ yàlàá piaw bɔɔ ndɔɔ « comme un lion quitte son repaire » (Jr 25,38) ; vannda piawnin ndi « elle sera abandonnée » (Es 7,16). Forme longue non relevée.</text></form></note>
  </entry>
  <entry id="pisio_1295">
    <lexical-unit><form lang="kqs"><text>pisio</text></form></lexical-unit>
    <trait name="status" value="attested"/>
    <variant><form lang="kqs"><text>pisi</text></form></variant>
    <variant><form lang="kqs"><text>pisinin</text></form></variant>
    <sense id="pisio_1295_s1">
      <grammatical-info value="Verb"/>
      <gloss lang="fr"><text>vendre</text></gloss>
      <gloss lang="en"><text>sell</text></gloss>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="6.8.4 Financial transaction"/>
    </sense>
    <field type="southern-kissi-sense"><form lang="en"><text>sell; give away freely</text></form></field>
    <note type="source"><form lang="en"><text>BKG: 38 occurrences, first GEN.31.15; Keita 1979, p. 113: Pisio; Childs 2000, p. 305: pìsìó</text></form></note>
  </entry>
  <entry id="pisultan_1296">
    <lexical-unit><form lang="kqs"><text>pisultan</text></form></lexical-unit>
    <trait name="noun-class" value="lan"/>
    <trait name="status" value="attested"/>
    <sense id="pisultan_1296_s1">
      <grammatical-info value="Noun"/>
      <gloss lang="fr"><text>jeu, jeux</text></gloss>
      <gloss lang="en"><text>play, games</text></gloss>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="4.2.6 Entertainment, recreation"/>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="4.2.7 Play, fun"/>
    </sense>
    <field type="southern-kissi-sense"><form lang="en"><text>play, joke, tease (also a verb)</text></form></field>
    <note type="source"><form lang="en"><text>BKG: 6 occurrences, first GEN.21.9; Keita 1979, p. 163: Pisultan; Childs 2000, p. 305: pìsúltáŋ</text></form></note>
  </entry>
  <entry id="pisultan_1297">
    <lexical-unit><form lang="kqs"><text>pisultan</text></form></lexical-unit>
    <trait name="status" value="attested"/>
    <variant><form lang="kqs"><text>pisul</text></form></variant>
    <variant><form lang="kqs"><text>pisulnin</text></form></variant>
    <sense id="pisultan_1297_s1">
      <grammatical-info value="Verb"/>
      <gloss lang="fr"><text>jouer, s'amuser</text></gloss>
      <gloss lang="en"><text>play</text></gloss>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="4.2.7 Play, fun"/>
    </sense>
    <field type="southern-kissi-sense"><form lang="en"><text>play, joke</text></form></field>
    <note type="source"><form lang="en"><text>BKG: 6 occurrences, first GEN.21.9; Keita 1979, p. 113: Pisultan; Childs 2000, p. 305: pìsúltáŋ</text></form></note>
  </entry>
  <entry id="píŋndo_1298">
    <lexical-unit><form lang="kqs"><text>píŋndo</text></form></lexical-unit>
    <trait name="noun-class" value="o"/>
    <trait name="status" value="attested"/>
    <field type="plural"><form lang="kqs"><text>piŋndan</text></form></field>
    <sense id="píŋndo_1298_s1">
      <grammatical-info value="Noun"/>
      <gloss lang="fr"><text>enclos, encerclement ; (luei … o píŋndo nin) assiéger, enfermer</text></gloss>
      <gloss lang="en"><text>enclosure, encirclement; (luei … o píŋndo nin) besiege, hem in</text></gloss>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="4.8.3 War"/>
    </sense>
    <field type="southern-kissi-sense"><form lang="en"><text>fence of palm-branch thatch, used for storing palm nuts</text></form></field>
    <note type="source"><form lang="en"><text>BKG: 5 occurrences, first PSA.17.11; Childs 2000, p. 303: píŋndó</text></form></note>
    <note><form lang="fr"><text>I lueinin niaa o píŋndo nin « je t'assiégerai » (Es 29,3) ; toosiaa piŋndan « élever des ouvrages de siège » (Ez 4,2).</text></form></note>
  </entry>
  <entry id="piɔlɔɔ_1299">
    <lexical-unit><form lang="kqs"><text>piɔlɔɔ</text></form></lexical-unit>
    <trait name="status" value="attested"/>
    <variant><form lang="kqs"><text>piɔl</text></form></variant>
    <variant><form lang="kqs"><text>pɛl</text></form></variant>
    <variant><form lang="kqs"><text>pial</text></form></variant>
    <variant><form lang="kqs"><text>pel</text></form></variant>
    <variant><form lang="kqs"><text>pialnin</text></form></variant>
    <variant><form lang="kqs"><text>piɔlnin</text></form></variant>
    <sense id="piɔlɔɔ_1299_s1">
      <grammatical-info value="Verb"/>
      <gloss lang="fr"><text>briser, casser, écraser ; prononcer (un nom)</text></gloss>
      <gloss lang="en"><text>break, crush; pronounce (a name)</text></gloss>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="7.8.1 Break"/>
    </sense>
    <note type="source"><form lang="en"><text>BKG: 16 occurrences, first GEN.48.20; Keita 1979, p. 116: Piölöö</text></form></note>
    <note><form lang="fr"><text>pel : radical négatif (EXO 12,46). diola pial « prononcer le nom » (EXO 20,7).</text></form></note>
  </entry>
  <entry id="piɔmaa_1300">
    <lexical-unit><form lang="kqs"><text>piɔmaa</text></form></lexical-unit>
    <trait name="status" value="attested"/>
    <sense id="piɔmaa_1300_s1">
      <grammatical-info value="Noun"/>
      <gloss lang="fr"><text>idoles, statues de dieux</text></gloss>
      <gloss lang="en"><text>idols, images of gods</text></gloss>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="4.9.8 Religious things"/>
    </sense>
    <note type="source"><form lang="en"><text>BKG: 175 occurrences, first GEN.31.19</text></form></note>
  </entry>
  <entry id="piɔ́mndo_1301">
    <lexical-unit><form lang="kqs"><text>piɔ́mndo</text></form></lexical-unit>
    <trait name="status" value="attested"/>
    <variant><form lang="kqs"><text>piɔ́m</text></form></variant>
    <sense id="piɔ́mndo_1301_s1">
      <grammatical-info value="Verb"/>
      <gloss lang="fr"><text>mourir ; la mort</text></gloss>
      <gloss lang="en"><text>die; death</text></gloss>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="2.6.6 Die"/>
    </sense>
    <note type="source"><form lang="en"><text>BKG: 492 occurrences, first GEN.2.17</text></form></note>
  </entry>
  <entry id="piɔndio_1302">
    <lexical-unit><form lang="kqs"><text>piɔndio</text></form></lexical-unit>
    <trait name="status" value="attested"/>
    <variant><form lang="kqs"><text>piɔndi</text></form></variant>
    <variant><form lang="kqs"><text>piɔndinin</text></form></variant>
    <sense id="piɔndio_1302_s1">
      <grammatical-info value="Verb"/>
      <gloss lang="fr"><text>tonner, gronder ; (piɔndi a caŋndo) éclater en sanglots</text></gloss>
      <gloss lang="en"><text>thunder, roar; (piɔndi a caŋndo) burst into tears</text></gloss>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="1.1.3 Weather"/>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="3.4.2 Feel bad"/>
    </sense>
    <field type="southern-kissi-sense"><form lang="en"><text>explode, pop (as corn)</text></form></field>
    <note type="source"><form lang="en"><text>BKG: 6 occurrences, first PSA.29.3; Childs 2000, p. 298: pìèndìóó</text></form></note>
    <note><form lang="fr"><text>Hala biilaa co piɔndio « le Dieu de gloire tonne » (Ps 29,3) ; mó piɔndi a caŋndo « il éclata en sanglots » (Gn 29,11).</text></form></note>
  </entry>
  <entry id="piɔsio_1303">
    <lexical-unit><form lang="kqs"><text>piɔsio</text></form></lexical-unit>
    <trait name="status" value="attested"/>
    <variant><form lang="kqs"><text>piɔsi</text></form></variant>
    <variant><form lang="kqs"><text>piɔsinin</text></form></variant>
    <sense id="piɔsio_1303_s1">
      <grammatical-info value="Verb"/>
      <gloss lang="fr"><text>se briser, voler en éclats, se fendre ; (bourgeon) éclater</text></gloss>
      <gloss lang="en"><text>break, shatter, split; (bud) burst open</text></gloss>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="7.8.1 Break"/>
    </sense>
    <field type="southern-kissi-sense"><form lang="en"><text>be broken, break by itself (esp. several things)</text></form></field>
    <note type="source"><form lang="en"><text>BKG: 4 occurrences, first 1KI.1.40; Childs 2000, p. 304: pìɔ̀sìó</text></form></note>
    <note><form lang="fr"><text>bolle ndɔlen le piɔsi « sa tête se brisa » (1 S 5,4) ; mɛɛ kpɛɛnɛi … piɔsi « comme se brise un pot de potier » (Es 30,14) ; pei lendei ken piɔsi « le bâton avait bourgeonné » (Nb 17,23). Apparenté à piɔlɔɔ « briser ».</text></form></note>
  </entry>
  <entry id="piɔu_1304">
    <lexical-unit><form lang="kqs"><text>piɔu</text></form></lexical-unit>
    <trait name="status" value="attested"/>
    <sense id="piɔu_1304_s1">
      <grammatical-info value="Verb"/>
      <gloss lang="fr"><text>monter, se remplir, déborder ; augmenter</text></gloss>
      <gloss lang="en"><text>rise, fill up, overflow; increase</text></gloss>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="1.3.2 Movement of water"/>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="8.1.8 Full"/>
    </sense>
    <field type="southern-kissi-sense"><form lang="en"><text>be full, lumpy or swollen</text></form></field>
    <note type="source"><form lang="en"><text>BKG: 8 occurrences, first GEN.7.18; Childs 2000, p. 304: pìɔ̀ɔ́</text></form></note>
    <note><form lang="fr"><text>taala kólaa nuu co piɔu « ma coupe déborde » (Ps 23,5) ; dɛ̀ndɔ̀ɔ́ va piɔu a mɛnndan « la barque se remplissait d'eau » (Mc 4,37) ; mɔnɛi kɔa a piɔu « le chagrin augmente » (Qo 1,18).</text></form></note>
  </entry>
  <entry id="piɔvan_1305">
    <lexical-unit><form lang="kqs"><text>piɔvan</text></form></lexical-unit>
    <trait name="status" value="attested"/>
    <sense id="piɔvan_1305_s1">
      <grammatical-info value="Verb"/>
      <gloss lang="fr"><text>se diviser, se séparer</text></gloss>
      <gloss lang="en"><text>be divided, divide (intr.)</text></gloss>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="7.8 Divide into pieces"/>
    </sense>
    <field type="southern-kissi-sense"><form lang="en"><text>share oneself, contribute one's time and effort</text></form></field>
    <note type="source"><form lang="en"><text>BKG: 37 occurrences, first GEN.2.10; Childs 2000, p. 304: pìɔ́ŋndó</text></form></note>
    <note><form lang="fr"><text>Moyen de piɔwvo.</text></form></note>
  </entry>
  <entry id="piɔwvo_1306">
    <lexical-unit><form lang="kqs"><text>piɔwvo</text></form></lexical-unit>
    <trait name="status" value="attested"/>
    <variant><form lang="kqs"><text>piɔw</text></form></variant>
    <sense id="piɔwvo_1306_s1">
      <grammatical-info value="Verb"/>
      <gloss lang="fr"><text>partager, diviser</text></gloss>
      <gloss lang="en"><text>divide, share out</text></gloss>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="7.8 Divide into pieces"/>
    </sense>
    <field type="southern-kissi-sense"><form lang="en"><text>distribute, share</text></form></field>
    <note type="source"><form lang="en"><text>BKG: 54 occurrences, first GEN.10.25; Childs 2000, p. 304: pìɔ̀ùwɔ́</text></form></note>
  </entry>
  <entry id="piɔŋndo_1307">
    <lexical-unit><form lang="kqs"><text>piɔŋndo</text></form></lexical-unit>
    <trait name="noun-class" value="o"/>
    <trait name="status" value="attested"/>
    <field type="plural"><form lang="kqs"><text>piɔŋndan</text></form></field>
    <variant><form lang="kqs"><text>piɔŋnda</text></form></variant>
    <sense id="piɔŋndo_1307_s1">
      <grammatical-info value="Noun"/>
      <gloss lang="fr"><text>furoncle, abcès</text></gloss>
      <gloss lang="en"><text>boil, abscess</text></gloss>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="2.5.6 Symptom of disease"/>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="2.5.2 Disease"/>
    </sense>
    <field type="southern-kissi-sense"><form lang="en"><text>a skin rash forming large pustules</text></form></field>
    <note type="source"><form lang="en"><text>BKG: 3 occurrences, first LEV.13.18; Childs 2000, p. 304: pìɔ̀mndó</text></form></note>
    <note><form lang="fr"><text>piɔŋnda lan la siŋnun pavii vɔɔnde « ce seront des furoncles qui se changeront en plaies » (Ex 9,9).</text></form></note>
  </entry>
  <entry id="piɔɔ_1308">
    <lexical-unit><form lang="kqs"><text>piɔɔ</text></form></lexical-unit>
    <trait name="status" value="attested"/>
    <sense id="piɔɔ_1308_s1">
      <grammatical-info value="Noun"/>
      <gloss lang="fr"><text>pluie</text></gloss>
      <gloss lang="en"><text>rain</text></gloss>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="1.1.3 Weather"/>
    </sense>
    <note type="source"><form lang="en"><text>BKG: 184 occurrences, first GEN.2.5</text></form></note>
  </entry>
  <entry id="piɔɔ bɛndoo_1309">
    <lexical-unit><form lang="kqs"><text>piɔɔ bɛndoo</text></form></lexical-unit>
    <trait name="status" value="attested"/>
    <sense id="piɔɔ bɛndoo_1309_s1">
      <grammatical-info value="Noun"/>
      <gloss lang="fr"><text>tornade ; forte pluie</text></gloss>
      <gloss lang="en"><text>tornado, rainstorm</text></gloss>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="1.1.3 Weather"/>
    </sense>
    <note type="source"><form lang="en"><text>Keita 1979, p. 155: Piöö bènduo</text></form></note>
    <note><form lang="fr"><text>Litt. « grande pluie ». Keita écrit bènduo ; la Bible bɛndoo (piɔɔ bɛndu-bɛndoo, 1KI.18.45).</text></form></note>
  </entry>
  <entry id="piɛilen_1310">
    <lexical-unit><form lang="kqs"><text>piɛilen</text></form></lexical-unit>
    <trait name="noun-class" value="len"/>
    <trait name="status" value="attested"/>
    <variant><form lang="kqs"><text>piɛile</text></form></variant>
    <sense id="piɛilen_1310_s1">
      <grammatical-info value="Noun"/>
      <gloss lang="fr"><text>prière, demande</text></gloss>
      <gloss lang="en"><text>prayer, request</text></gloss>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="4.9.5 Practice religion"/>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="3.3.2 Request"/>
    </sense>
    <note type="source"><form lang="en"><text>BKG: 97 occurrences, first GEN.4.26; Childs 2000, p. 298: pìèlɛ́ŋ</text></form></note>
  </entry>
  <entry id="piɛiyo_1311">
    <lexical-unit><form lang="kqs"><text>piɛiyo</text></form></lexical-unit>
    <trait name="status" value="attested"/>
    <variant><form lang="kqs"><text>piɛi</text></form></variant>
    <sense id="piɛiyo_1311_s1">
      <grammatical-info value="Verb"/>
      <gloss lang="fr"><text>prier ; demander, supplier</text></gloss>
      <gloss lang="en"><text>pray; ask, beg</text></gloss>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="4.9.5 Practice religion"/>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="3.3.2 Request"/>
    </sense>
    <field type="southern-kissi-sense"><form lang="en"><text>beg; (benefactive) pray or ask on someone's behalf</text></form></field>
    <note type="source"><form lang="en"><text>BKG: 107 occurrences, first DEU.12.5; Childs 2000, p. 298: pìèyɔ́</text></form></note>
  </entry>
  <entry id="polalen_1312">
    <lexical-unit><form lang="kqs"><text>polalen</text></form></lexical-unit>
    <trait name="noun-class" value="len"/>
    <trait name="status" value="attested"/>
    <variant><form lang="kqs"><text>polale</text></form></variant>
    <variant><form lang="kqs"><text>polama</text></form></variant>
    <sense id="polalen_1312_s1">
      <grammatical-info value="Noun"/>
      <gloss lang="fr"><text>lignée, descendance, tribu ; généalogie</text></gloss>
      <gloss lang="en"><text>lineage, descendants, tribe; generations</text></gloss>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="4.1.9 Kinship"/>
    </sense>
    <note type="source"><form lang="en"><text>BKG: 40 occurrences, first EXO.40.23</text></form></note>
    <note><form lang="fr"><text>polale Noe len « la descendance de Noé » ; au pluriel, forme radicale polama (polama Israɛlla « les tribus d'Israël »).</text></form></note>
  </entry>
  <entry id="polon_1313">
    <lexical-unit><form lang="kqs"><text>polon</text></form></lexical-unit>
    <trait name="status" value="attested"/>
    <sense id="polon_1313_s1">
      <grammatical-info value="Adverb"/>
      <gloss lang="fr"><text>dehors, au loin</text></gloss>
      <gloss lang="en"><text>outside, away</text></gloss>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="8.5.2 Direction"/>
    </sense>
    <field type="southern-kissi-sense"><form lang="en"><text>far, high up, far away; deep</text></form></field>
    <note type="source"><form lang="en"><text>BKG: 102 occurrences, first GEN.21.10; Childs 2000, p. 306: pólóŋ</text></form></note>
  </entry>
  <entry id="pondaa_1314">
    <lexical-unit><form lang="kqs"><text>pondaa</text></form></lexical-unit>
    <trait name="noun-class" value="o"/>
    <trait name="status" value="respelled"/>
    <sense id="pondaa_1314_s1">
      <grammatical-info value="Noun"/>
      <gloss lang="fr"><text>fard noir</text></gloss>
      <gloss lang="en"><text>black make-up paint</text></gloss>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="5.4.2 Cosmetics"/>
    </sense>
    <note type="source"><form lang="en"><text>Keita 1979, p. 144: Pondaa</text></form></note>
    <note><form lang="fr"><text>Même racine probable que pondalen « marque, sceau » (Gn 4,15).</text></form></note>
  </entry>
  <entry id="pondaa sɛvaa_1315">
    <lexical-unit><form lang="kqs"><text>pondaa sɛvaa</text></form></lexical-unit>
    <trait name="status" value="respelled"/>
    <sense id="pondaa sɛvaa_1315_s1">
      <grammatical-info value="Noun"/>
      <gloss lang="fr"><text>encre</text></gloss>
      <gloss lang="en"><text>ink</text></gloss>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="3.5.7 Reading and writing"/>
    </sense>
    <note type="source"><form lang="en"><text>Keita 1979, p. 159: Pondaa sèvaa</text></form></note>
    <note><form lang="fr"><text>sɛvaa « écrire » est attesté (Ex 28,36).</text></form></note>
  </entry>
  <entry id="pondalen_1316">
    <lexical-unit><form lang="kqs"><text>pondalen</text></form></lexical-unit>
    <trait name="noun-class" value="len"/>
    <trait name="status" value="attested"/>
    <variant><form lang="kqs"><text>pondale</text></form></variant>
    <sense id="pondalen_1316_s1">
      <grammatical-info value="Noun"/>
      <gloss lang="fr"><text>marque, signe ; sceau</text></gloss>
      <gloss lang="en"><text>mark, sign; seal</text></gloss>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="3.5.6 Sign, symbol"/>
    </sense>
    <note type="source"><form lang="en"><text>BKG: 15 occurrences, first GEN.4.15</text></form></note>
  </entry>
  <entry id="pondoo_1317">
    <lexical-unit><form lang="kqs"><text>pondoo</text></form></lexical-unit>
    <trait name="status" value="respelled"/>
    <sense id="pondoo_1317_s1">
      <grammatical-info value="Noun"/>
      <gloss lang="fr"><text>janvier</text></gloss>
      <gloss lang="en"><text>January</text></gloss>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="8.4.4 Telling time"/>
    </sense>
    <note type="source"><form lang="en"><text>Keita 1979, p. 152: Pondoo</text></form></note>
  </entry>
  <entry id="pongan_1318">
    <lexical-unit><form lang="kqs"><text>pongan</text></form></lexical-unit>
    <trait name="status" value="attested"/>
    <sense id="pongan_1318_s1">
      <grammatical-info value="Noun"/>
      <gloss lang="fr"><text>taches, mouchetures (du pelage)</text></gloss>
      <gloss lang="en"><text>spots, speckles (of an animal's coat)</text></gloss>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="8.3.3 Light"/>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="1.6.2 Parts of an animal"/>
    </sense>
    <note type="source"><form lang="en"><text>BKG: 7 occurrences, first GEN.30.35</text></form></note>
    <note><form lang="fr"><text>cɔlu oo cɔlu nɔ pongan « toute bête qui avait des taches » (Gn 30,35).</text></form></note>
  </entry>
  <entry id="poo_1319">
    <lexical-unit><form lang="kqs"><text>poo</text></form></lexical-unit>
    <trait name="noun-class" value="o"/>
    <trait name="status" value="attested"/>
    <field type="plural"><form lang="kqs"><text>poaa</text></form></field>
    <variant><form lang="kqs"><text>po</text></form></variant>
    <sense id="poo_1319_s1">
      <grammatical-info value="Noun"/>
      <gloss lang="fr"><text>fils, enfant (mâle) ; (pl.) fils, descendants</text></gloss>
      <gloss lang="en"><text>son, (male) child; (pl.) sons, descendants</text></gloss>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="4.1.9 Kinship"/>
    </sense>
    <field type="southern-kissi-sense"><form lang="en"><text>boy, youth</text></form></field>
    <note type="source"><form lang="en"><text>BKG: 87 occurrences, first GEN.4.26; Childs 2000, p. 307: pòó</text></form></note>
    <note><form lang="fr"><text>Forme radicale po : po ndɔɔ « son fils », po vanalanɔɔ « le fils de la femme » (Gn 3,15) ; poaa Israɛl « les Israélites ». Vocatif ponndo « mon fils ! » (Gn 43,29) ; pole pilɛlen « fils unique » (Gn 22,12 ; Childs póléŋ « only male child »).</text></form></note>
  </entry>
  <entry id="poolan_1320">
    <lexical-unit><form lang="kqs"><text>poolan</text></form></lexical-unit>
    <trait name="noun-class" value="lan"/>
    <trait name="status" value="attested"/>
    <variant><form lang="kqs"><text>poola</text></form></variant>
    <sense id="poolan_1320_s1">
      <grammatical-info value="Noun"/>
      <gloss lang="fr"><text>excréments, fiente, bouse</text></gloss>
      <gloss lang="en"><text>dung, excrement</text></gloss>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="2.2.8 Defecate, feces"/>
    </sense>
    <note type="source"><form lang="en"><text>BKG: 1 occurrences, first MAL.2.3; Childs 2000, p. 307: pòòléŋ</text></form></note>
  </entry>
  <entry id="poombɔɔ_1321">
    <lexical-unit><form lang="kqs"><text>poombɔɔ</text></form></lexical-unit>
    <trait name="status" value="attested"/>
    <field type="plural"><form lang="kqs"><text>poambɔa</text></form></field>
    <variant><form lang="kqs"><text>poombɔ</text></form></variant>
    <sense id="poombɔɔ_1321_s1">
      <grammatical-info value="Noun"/>
      <gloss lang="fr"><text>garçon, jeune homme</text></gloss>
      <gloss lang="en"><text>boy, young man</text></gloss>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="2.6.4 Stage of life"/>
    </sense>
    <field type="southern-kissi-sense"><form lang="en"><text>boy, small boy; son, male child</text></form></field>
    <note type="source"><form lang="en"><text>BKG: 87 occurrences, first GEN.21.12; Childs 2000, p. 307: pòómbɔ̀ɔ́</text></form></note>
  </entry>
  <entry id="poondaa_1322">
    <lexical-unit><form lang="kqs"><text>poondaa</text></form></lexical-unit>
    <trait name="status" value="attested"/>
    <variant><form lang="kqs"><text>poonda</text></form></variant>
    <variant><form lang="kqs"><text>poondan</text></form></variant>
    <variant><form lang="kqs"><text>poondanin</text></form></variant>
    <sense id="poondaa_1322_s1">
      <grammatical-info value="Verb"/>
      <gloss lang="fr"><text>enlever, arracher, prendre de force ; (poondan) s'échapper</text></gloss>
      <gloss lang="en"><text>take away, snatch, seize by force; (poondan) escape</text></gloss>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="7.3.2 Move something in a direction"/>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="7.4.3 Get"/>
    </sense>
    <field type="southern-kissi-sense"><form lang="en"><text>take away, pull off; also shuck; (middle) slip out</text></form></field>
    <note type="source"><form lang="en"><text>BKG: 5 occurrences, first JDG.11.23; Childs 2000, p. 307: pòòndàá</text></form></note>
    <note><form lang="fr"><text>Verbe de base de poondiaa. I poondanin Salomɔn masalen … o ba « j'arracherai le royaume des mains de Salomon » (1 R 11,34) ; Yalaa timbinndo, mí n poondan « le filet s'est rompu et nous nous sommes échappés » (Ps 124,7).</text></form></note>
  </entry>
  <entry id="poondiaa_1323">
    <lexical-unit><form lang="kqs"><text>poondiaa</text></form></lexical-unit>
    <trait name="status" value="attested"/>
    <sense id="poondiaa_1323_s1">
      <grammatical-info value="Verb"/>
      <gloss lang="fr"><text>emmener (comme butin, en captivité), enlever, confisquer</text></gloss>
      <gloss lang="en"><text>carry off (as plunder, captive), take away, confiscate</text></gloss>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="7.3.3 Take somewhere"/>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="4.8.3 War"/>
    </sense>
    <field type="southern-kissi-sense"><form lang="en"><text>take away (plural action); shuck</text></form></field>
    <note type="source"><form lang="en"><text>BKG: 70 occurrences, first NUM.14.3; Childs 2000, p. 307: pòòndìá</text></form></note>
  </entry>
  <entry id="poonpoon_1324">
    <lexical-unit><form lang="kqs"><text>poonpoon</text></form></lexical-unit>
    <trait name="status" value="attested"/>
    <sense id="poonpoon_1324_s1">
      <grammatical-info value="Noun"/>
      <gloss lang="fr"><text>colombe</text></gloss>
      <gloss lang="en"><text>dove</text></gloss>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="1.6.1 Types of animals"/>
    </sense>
    <note type="source"><form lang="en"><text>BKG: 13 occurrences, first GEN.8.9</text></form></note>
  </entry>
  <entry id="poonpoondo_1325">
    <lexical-unit><form lang="kqs"><text>poonpoondo</text></form></lexical-unit>
    <trait name="noun-class" value="o"/>
    <trait name="status" value="attested"/>
    <field type="plural"><form lang="kqs"><text>poonpoonda</text></form></field>
    <sense id="poonpoondo_1325_s1">
      <grammatical-info value="Noun"/>
      <gloss lang="fr"><text>pigeon vert ; colombe</text></gloss>
      <gloss lang="en"><text>green pigeon; dove</text></gloss>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="1.6.1 Types of animals"/>
    </sense>
    <note type="source"><form lang="en"><text>BKG: 6 occurrences, first GEN.8.8; Keita 1979, p. 137: Poonpoonndo</text></form></note>
    <note><form lang="fr"><text>Keita : pigeon vert ; la Bible l'emploie pour la colombe.</text></form></note>
  </entry>
  <entry id="poopoo_1326">
    <lexical-unit><form lang="kqs"><text>poopoo</text></form></lexical-unit>
    <trait name="status" value="check"/>
    <sense id="poopoo_1326_s1">
      <grammatical-info value="Noun"/>
      <gloss lang="fr"><text>insolence, outrage ; (vana poopoo) vaurien, effronté</text></gloss>
      <gloss lang="en"><text>insolence, disgrace; (vana poopoo) scoundrel, brazen person</text></gloss>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="4.3 Behavior"/>
    </sense>
    <note><form lang="fr"><text>sui … poopoo « outrager, déshonorer, importuner » (Dt 22,19 ; Rt 2,9) ; vanalanɔ poopoo « femme effrontée » (Pr 7,11). Sens à confirmer.</text></form></note>
  </entry>
  <entry id="pooɲɛi_1327">
    <lexical-unit><form lang="kqs"><text>pooɲɛi</text></form></lexical-unit>
    <trait name="status" value="attested"/>
    <variant><form lang="kqs"><text>pooɲɛiya</text></form></variant>
    <variant><form lang="kqs"><text>pooɲɛila</text></form></variant>
    <variant><form lang="kqs"><text>pooɲɛilen</text></form></variant>
    <sense id="pooɲɛi_1327_s1">
      <grammatical-info value="Adjective"/>
      <gloss lang="fr"><text>tacheté, moucheté</text></gloss>
      <gloss lang="en"><text>speckled, spotted</text></gloss>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="8.3.3 Light"/>
    </sense>
    <field type="southern-kissi-sense"><form lang="en"><text>spotted, colourful, multicoloured</text></form></field>
    <note type="source"><form lang="en"><text>BKG: 2 occurrences, first GEN.30.33; Childs 2000, p. 307: pòɲéí-</text></form></note>
    <note><form lang="fr"><text>cɔlua pooɲɛiya « les bêtes tachetées » (Gn 30,32).</text></form></note>
  </entry>
  <entry id="powvo_1328">
    <lexical-unit><form lang="kqs"><text>powvo</text></form></lexical-unit>
    <trait name="noun-class" value="o"/>
    <trait name="status" value="attested"/>
    <field type="plural"><form lang="kqs"><text>powtan</text></form></field>
    <sense id="powvo_1328_s1">
      <grammatical-info value="Noun"/>
      <gloss lang="fr"><text>pierre, caillou</text></gloss>
      <gloss lang="en"><text>stone, pebble</text></gloss>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="1.2.2 Substance, matter"/>
    </sense>
    <field type="southern-kissi-sense"><form lang="en"><text>rock, large stone; battery</text></form></field>
    <note type="source"><form lang="en"><text>BKG: 60 occurrences, first GEN.28.11; Keita 1979, p. 155: Powvo; Childs 2000, p. 308: pòùwó</text></form></note>
  </entry>
  <entry id="poŋ_1329">
    <lexical-unit><form lang="kqs"><text>poŋ</text></form></lexical-unit>
    <trait name="status" value="attested"/>
    <sense id="poŋ_1329_s1">
      <grammatical-info value="Ideophone"/>
      <gloss lang="fr"><text>dur, ferme, solide</text></gloss>
      <gloss lang="en"><text>hard, firm, solid</text></gloss>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="9.2.8 Ideophones"/>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="8.3.2 Texture"/>
    </sense>
    <note type="source"><form lang="en"><text>BKG: 5 occurrences, first NUM.24.21</text></form></note>
    <note><form lang="fr"><text>mɛmma … ma kendu poŋ « les eaux gèlent » (Jb 37,10) ; calta niaalan la co lakala poŋ « ta demeure est solide » (Nb 24,21).</text></form></note>
  </entry>
  <entry id="puapilɛ_1330">
    <lexical-unit><form lang="kqs"><text>puapilɛ</text></form></lexical-unit>
    <trait name="status" value="attested"/>
    <field type="plural"><form lang="kqs"><text>puapilɛa</text></form></field>
    <sense id="puapilɛ_1330_s1">
      <grammatical-info value="Noun"/>
      <gloss lang="fr"><text>prochain, compagnon ; frère (de la même communauté)</text></gloss>
      <gloss lang="en"><text>neighbour, fellow; brother (fellow member)</text></gloss>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="4.1.4 Neighbor"/>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="4.1.1 Friend"/>
    </sense>
    <note type="source"><form lang="en"><text>BKG: 209 occurrences, first GEN.9.5</text></form></note>
  </entry>
  <entry id="puilen_1331">
    <lexical-unit><form lang="kqs"><text>puilen</text></form></lexical-unit>
    <trait name="noun-class" value="len"/>
    <trait name="status" value="attested"/>
    <variant><form lang="kqs"><text>puile</text></form></variant>
    <sense id="puilen_1331_s1">
      <grammatical-info value="Noun"/>
      <gloss lang="fr"><text>queue</text></gloss>
      <gloss lang="en"><text>tail</text></gloss>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="1.6.2 Parts of an animal"/>
    </sense>
    <field type="southern-kissi-sense"><form lang="en"><text>a brush of tied grass used by a praise singer, often replaced by a cow's tail</text></form></field>
    <note type="source"><form lang="en"><text>BKG: 6 occurrences, first EXO.4.4; Childs 2000, p. 311: pùìléŋ</text></form></note>
    <note><form lang="fr"><text>puile ndɔlen « sa queue (grasse) » (Lv 3,9).</text></form></note>
  </entry>
  <entry id="puiyaa_1332">
    <lexical-unit><form lang="kqs"><text>puiyaa</text></form></lexical-unit>
    <trait name="status" value="attested"/>
    <variant><form lang="kqs"><text>pui</text></form></variant>
    <variant><form lang="kqs"><text>puinin</text></form></variant>
    <sense id="puiyaa_1332_s1">
      <grammatical-info value="Verb"/>
      <gloss lang="fr"><text>pousser, verdir, repousser ; verdure</text></gloss>
      <gloss lang="en"><text>sprout, grow green, shoot again; greenery</text></gloss>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="1.5.6 Growth of plants"/>
    </sense>
    <field type="southern-kissi-sense"><form lang="en"><text>sprout new growth, grow</text></form></field>
    <note type="source"><form lang="en"><text>BKG: 47 occurrences, first GEN.13.10; Childs 2000, p. 311: pùìyó</text></form></note>
    <note><form lang="fr"><text>o muungu vɛlɛ o pui « il repousse » (Jb 14,7) ; dɛɛla … va o puiyaa ɲɛkɛndɛi « la plaine était bien arrosée, verdoyante » (Gn 13,10).</text></form></note>
  </entry>
  <entry id="puiyo_1333">
    <lexical-unit><form lang="kqs"><text>puiyo</text></form></lexical-unit>
    <trait name="noun-class" value="o"/>
    <trait name="status" value="attested"/>
    <sense id="puiyo_1333_s1">
      <grammatical-info value="Noun"/>
      <gloss lang="fr"><text>paille</text></gloss>
      <gloss lang="en"><text>straw</text></gloss>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="1.5.3 Grass, herb, vine"/>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="6.2.6 Process harvest"/>
    </sense>
    <field type="southern-kissi-sense"><form lang="en"><text>new sprouts; thatch, grass cut for thatching</text></form></field>
    <note type="source"><form lang="en"><text>BKG: 5 occurrences, first JDG.19.19; Keita 1979, p. 140: Puiyo; Childs 2000, p. 311: pùìyó</text></form></note>
  </entry>
  <entry id="pulen_1334">
    <lexical-unit><form lang="kqs"><text>pulen</text></form></lexical-unit>
    <trait name="noun-class" value="len"/>
    <trait name="status" value="respelled"/>
    <variant><form lang="kqs"><text>pule</text></form></variant>
    <sense id="pulen_1334_s1">
      <grammatical-info value="Noun"/>
      <gloss lang="fr"><text>nombril ; cordon ombilical</text></gloss>
      <gloss lang="en"><text>navel; umbilical cord</text></gloss>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="2.1.2 Torso"/>
    </sense>
    <note type="source"><form lang="en"><text>Keita 1979, p. 132: Pulen; Childs 2000, p. 311: pùléŋ</text></form></note>
    <note><form lang="fr"><text>Forme radicale pule attestée (Ez 16,4 ; Ct 7,3).</text></form></note>
  </entry>
  <entry id="pulon_1335">
    <lexical-unit><form lang="kqs"><text>pulon</text></form></lexical-unit>
    <trait name="status" value="attested"/>
    <sense id="pulon_1335_s1">
      <grammatical-info value="Noun"/>
      <gloss lang="fr"><text>entrailles, intestins</text></gloss>
      <gloss lang="en"><text>entrails, intestines</text></gloss>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="2.1.8 Internal organs"/>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="1.6.2 Parts of an animal"/>
    </sense>
    <field type="southern-kissi-sense"><form lang="en"><text>stomach, intestines (plural pùlóŋ); also a woman's labour stage, a strip of cloth</text></form></field>
    <note type="source"><form lang="en"><text>BKG: 11 occurrences, first LEV.3.3; Childs 2000, p. 311: pùléí</text></form></note>
    <note><form lang="fr"><text>cuɛima kumbu pulon « la graisse qui couvre les entrailles » (Lv 3,3). Voir pulen « nombril ».</text></form></note>
  </entry>
  <entry id="pulta_1336">
    <lexical-unit><form lang="kqs"><text>pulta</text></form></lexical-unit>
    <trait name="status" value="attested"/>
    <field type="plural"><form lang="kqs"><text>pultan</text></form></field>
    <sense id="pulta_1336_s1">
      <grammatical-info value="Noun"/>
      <gloss lang="fr"><text>cendre</text></gloss>
      <gloss lang="en"><text>ash</text></gloss>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="5.5 Fire"/>
    </sense>
    <note type="source"><form lang="en"><text>BKG: 15 occurrences, first EXO.9.8; Childs 2000, p. 312: pùltáŋ</text></form></note>
  </entry>
  <entry id="pulɔn sɛllo_1337">
    <lexical-unit><form lang="kqs"><text>pulɔn sɛllo</text></form></lexical-unit>
    <trait name="status" value="respelled"/>
    <sense id="pulɔn sɛllo_1337_s1">
      <grammatical-info value="Noun"/>
      <gloss lang="fr"><text>ablution</text></gloss>
      <gloss lang="en"><text>ritual ablution</text></gloss>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="4.9.5 Practice religion"/>
    </sense>
    <note type="source"><form lang="en"><text>Keita 1979, p. 150: Pulön sèllo</text></form></note>
  </entry>
  <entry id="pulɔnndo_1338">
    <lexical-unit><form lang="kqs"><text>pulɔnndo</text></form></lexical-unit>
    <trait name="status" value="attested"/>
    <variant><form lang="kqs"><text>pulun</text></form></variant>
    <sense id="pulɔnndo_1338_s1">
      <grammatical-info value="Verb"/>
      <gloss lang="fr"><text>se laver</text></gloss>
      <gloss lang="en"><text>wash oneself</text></gloss>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="5.6.2 Bathe"/>
    </sense>
    <note type="source"><form lang="en"><text>BKG: 7 occurrences, first EXO.2.5; Keita 1979, p. 115: Pulönndo</text></form></note>
    <note><form lang="fr"><text>Moyen de pulɔɔ.</text></form></note>
  </entry>
  <entry id="pulɔɔ_1339">
    <lexical-unit><form lang="kqs"><text>pulɔɔ</text></form></lexical-unit>
    <trait name="status" value="attested"/>
    <variant><form lang="kqs"><text>pulu</text></form></variant>
    <variant><form lang="kqs"><text>pilu</text></form></variant>
    <sense id="pulɔɔ_1339_s1">
      <grammatical-info value="Verb"/>
      <gloss lang="fr"><text>laver (personnes, corps)</text></gloss>
      <gloss lang="en"><text>wash (people, body)</text></gloss>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="5.6.2 Bathe"/>
    </sense>
    <field type="southern-kissi-sense"><form lang="en"><text>wash, bathe</text></form></field>
    <note type="source"><form lang="en"><text>BKG: 23 occurrences, first GEN.18.4; Keita 1979, p. 115: Pulöö; Childs 2000, p. 312: pùlɔ̀ɔ́</text></form></note>
    <note><form lang="fr"><text>pilu : radical négatif (MRK 7,2).</text></form></note>
  </entry>
  <entry id="pum_1340">
    <lexical-unit><form lang="kqs"><text>pum</text></form></lexical-unit>
    <trait name="status" value="attested"/>
    <sense id="pum_1340_s1">
      <grammatical-info value="Determiner"/>
      <gloss lang="fr"><text>un certain, un</text></gloss>
      <gloss lang="en"><text>a certain, some</text></gloss>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="8.1 Quantity"/>
    </sense>
    <field type="southern-kissi-sense"><form lang="en"><text>also 'a few, part, a little'</text></form></field>
    <note type="source"><form lang="en"><text>BKG: 1454 occurrences, first GEN.2.10; Childs 2000, p. 312: pùm</text></form></note>
  </entry>
  <entry id="pumbu_1341">
    <lexical-unit><form lang="kqs"><text>pumbu</text></form></lexical-unit>
    <trait name="status" value="check"/>
    <sense id="pumbu_1341_s1">
      <grammatical-info value="Noun"/>
      <gloss lang="fr"><text>lieu fixe, établissement (icali o pumbu « demeurer à un endroit fixe »)</text></gloss>
      <gloss lang="en"><text>settled place (icali o pumbu 'live in a fixed place')</text></gloss>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="5.9 Live, stay"/>
    </sense>
    <note><form lang="fr"><text>A ve lɛnin icali o pumbú le « tu ne demeureras nulle part (tu seras errant) » (Gn 4,12) ; vanaa cel o pumbu le « les nomades » (Jg 8,11). Aussi écrit pumbú. Sens à confirmer.</text></form></note>
  </entry>
  <entry id="pundaa_1342">
    <lexical-unit><form lang="kqs"><text>pundaa</text></form></lexical-unit>
    <trait name="noun-class" value="o"/>
    <trait name="status" value="attested"/>
    <sense id="pundaa_1342_s1">
      <grammatical-info value="Noun"/>
      <gloss lang="fr"><text>cécité, vue voilée</text></gloss>
      <gloss lang="en"><text>blindness, dimness of sight</text></gloss>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="2.5.4 Disabled"/>
    </sense>
    <field type="southern-kissi-sense"><form lang="en"><text>white filmy growth that causes cataracts and blindness</text></form></field>
    <note type="source"><form lang="en"><text>BKG: 7 occurrences, first GEN.27.1; Childs 2000, p. 312: púndáá</text></form></note>
    <note><form lang="fr"><text>pundaa cal ndu o lahɔl « ses yeux s'étaient affaiblis » (Gn 27,1).</text></form></note>
  </entry>
  <entry id="pungaa_1343">
    <lexical-unit><form lang="kqs"><text>pungaa</text></form></lexical-unit>
    <trait name="status" value="attested"/>
    <variant><form lang="kqs"><text>punga</text></form></variant>
    <variant><form lang="kqs"><text>pungapungaa</text></form></variant>
    <sense id="pungaa_1343_s1">
      <grammatical-info value="Verb"/>
      <gloss lang="fr"><text>piller, ravir ; pillage, butin</text></gloss>
      <gloss lang="en"><text>plunder, loot; plunder, spoil</text></gloss>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="4.8.3 War"/>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="7.4.3 Get"/>
    </sense>
    <field type="southern-kissi-sense"><form lang="en"><text>fight or squabble over something (e.g. food); also blossom</text></form></field>
    <note type="source"><form lang="en"><text>BKG: 5 occurrences, first 1SA.14.48; Childs 2000, p. 313: pùŋàá</text></form></note>
    <note><form lang="fr"><text>vannda punga ɲɛm naan « on a pillé nos biens » (Esd 9,7) ; siŋnun pungapungaa « devenir une proie » (Ez 26,5 ; 34,22).</text></form></note>
  </entry>
  <entry id="puuloo_1344">
    <lexical-unit><form lang="kqs"><text>puuloo</text></form></lexical-unit>
    <trait name="noun-class" value="o"/>
    <trait name="status" value="attested"/>
    <variant><form lang="kqs"><text>puulu</text></form></variant>
    <sense id="puuloo_1344_s1">
      <grammatical-info value="Noun"/>
      <gloss lang="fr"><text>terre, sol ; poussière ; boue, argile</text></gloss>
      <gloss lang="en"><text>earth, soil, ground; dust ; dust; mud, clay</text></gloss>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="1.2.2 Substance, matter"/>
    </sense>
    <field type="southern-kissi-sense"><form lang="en"><text>mud, dirt, stoneless soil; mortar</text></form></field>
    <note type="source"><form lang="en"><text>BKG: 51 occurrences, first GEN.2.7; Keita 1979, p. 155: Puuluo; Childs 2000, p. 313: pùùlòó</text></form></note>
    <note><form lang="fr"><text>Keita écrit Puuluo ; la Bible puuloo.</text></form></note>
  </entry>
  <entry id="puundulen_1345">
    <lexical-unit><form lang="kqs"><text>puundulen</text></form></lexical-unit>
    <trait name="noun-class" value="len"/>
    <trait name="status" value="respelled"/>
    <field type="plural"><form lang="kqs"><text>puundun</text></form></field>
    <variant><form lang="kqs"><text>puundule</text></form></variant>
    <sense id="puundulen_1345_s1">
      <grammatical-info value="Noun"/>
      <gloss lang="fr"><text>racine</text></gloss>
      <gloss lang="en"><text>root</text></gloss>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="1.5.5 Parts of a plant"/>
    </sense>
    <note type="source"><form lang="en"><text>Keita 1979, p. 140: Puundulen; Childs 2000, p. 314: pùùndúléŋ</text></form></note>
    <note><form lang="fr"><text>La Bible a la forme radicale puundule (ISA.53.2) et le pluriel puundun (2KI.19.30).</text></form></note>
  </entry>
  <entry id="puusiaa_1346">
    <lexical-unit><form lang="kqs"><text>puusiaa</text></form></lexical-unit>
    <trait name="status" value="attested"/>
    <variant><form lang="kqs"><text>puusian</text></form></variant>
    <sense id="puusiaa_1346_s1">
      <grammatical-info value="Verb"/>
      <gloss lang="fr"><text>disperser, déranger</text></gloss>
      <gloss lang="en"><text>scatter, disperse</text></gloss>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="7.5 Arrange"/>
    </sense>
    <field type="southern-kissi-sense"><form lang="en"><text>scatter, spread about</text></form></field>
    <note type="source"><form lang="en"><text>BKG: 85 occurrences, first GEN.11.8; Keita 1979, p. 113: Puusiaa; Childs 2000, p. 314: pùùsìá</text></form></note>
    <note><form lang="fr"><text>Moyen puusian « se disperser » (1SA 13,8).</text></form></note>
  </entry>
  <entry id="puusianɔɔ_1347">
    <lexical-unit><form lang="kqs"><text>puusianɔɔ</text></form></lexical-unit>
    <trait name="noun-class" value="o"/>
    <trait name="status" value="check"/>
    <sense id="puusianɔɔ_1347_s1">
      <grammatical-info value="Noun"/>
      <gloss lang="fr"><text>réactionnaire (Keita)</text></gloss>
      <gloss lang="en"><text>reactionary (Keita)</text></gloss>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="4.8 Conflict"/>
    </sense>
    <note type="source"><form lang="en"><text>Keita 1979, p. 148: Puusianöö</text></form></note>
    <note><form lang="fr"><text>La Bible a puusiaa « disperser » (Gn 11,8) ; le sens exact du dérivé est à confirmer.</text></form></note>
  </entry>
  <entry id="puuvo_1348">
    <lexical-unit><form lang="kqs"><text>puuvo</text></form></lexical-unit>
    <trait name="status" value="attested"/>
    <variant><form lang="kqs"><text>puu</text></form></variant>
    <variant><form lang="kqs"><text>puunin</text></form></variant>
    <variant><form lang="kqs"><text>puunun</text></form></variant>
    <variant><form lang="kqs"><text>puununnin</text></form></variant>
    <sense id="puuvo_1348_s1">
      <grammatical-info value="Verb"/>
      <gloss lang="fr"><text>prendre, enlever, arracher ; reprendre, récupérer</text></gloss>
      <gloss lang="en"><text>take, take away, snatch; take back, recover</text></gloss>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="7.4.3 Get"/>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="7.3.2 Move something in a direction"/>
    </sense>
    <field type="southern-kissi-sense"><form lang="en"><text>take away, seize, snatch; also become engaged to, hire</text></form></field>
    <note type="source"><form lang="en"><text>BKG: 3 occurrences, first ISA.10.2; Childs 2000, p. 315: pùùwó</text></form></note>
    <note><form lang="fr"><text>Mó puu vɛlɛ Lɔt « il reprit aussi Lot » (Gn 14,16) ; buɛyaa Abimelɛk-a ndáà puu a paa-kala « dont les serviteurs d'Abimélek s'étaient emparés » (Gn 21,25) ; puunun « s'emparer, être enlevé ».</text></form></note>
  </entry>
  <entry id="púvɔ́ɔ́_1349">
    <lexical-unit><form lang="kqs"><text>púvɔ́ɔ́</text></form></lexical-unit>
    <trait name="noun-class" value="o"/>
    <trait name="status" value="attested"/>
    <field type="plural"><form lang="kqs"><text>púwvɛa</text></form></field>
    <variant><form lang="kqs"><text>púvɛ</text></form></variant>
    <sense id="púvɔ́ɔ́_1349_s1">
      <grammatical-info value="Noun"/>
      <gloss lang="fr"><text>gazelle, chevreuil</text></gloss>
      <gloss lang="en"><text>gazelle, deer</text></gloss>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="1.6.1 Types of animals"/>
    </sense>
    <note type="source"><form lang="en"><text>BKG: 6 occurrences, first DEU.12.15</text></form></note>
    <note><form lang="fr"><text>maa púvɛ « comme une gazelle » (2 S 2,18 ; Ct 2,17).</text></form></note>
  </entry>
  <entry id="púŋ_1350">
    <lexical-unit><form lang="kqs"><text>púŋ</text></form></lexical-unit>
    <trait name="status" value="attested"/>
    <sense id="púŋ_1350_s1">
      <grammatical-info value="Ideophone"/>
      <gloss lang="fr"><text>(idiiyo púŋ) de grand matin</text></gloss>
      <gloss lang="en"><text>(idiiyo púŋ) very early in the morning</text></gloss>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="9.2.8 Ideophones"/>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="8.4.1 Period of time"/>
    </sense>
    <note type="source"><form lang="en"><text>BKG: 67 occurrences, first GEN.19.27</text></form></note>
  </entry>
  <entry id="pɔ́_1351">
    <lexical-unit><form lang="kqs"><text>pɔ́</text></form></lexical-unit>
    <trait name="status" value="attested"/>
    <variant><form lang="kqs"><text>pɔ́-pɔ́</text></form></variant>
    <sense id="pɔ́_1351_s1">
      <grammatical-info value="Adverb"/>
      <gloss lang="fr"><text>loin, très loin ; très haut</text></gloss>
      <gloss lang="en"><text>far, far away; very high</text></gloss>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="8.2.6 Distance"/>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="8.6.2 Top"/>
    </sense>
    <field type="southern-kissi-sense"><form lang="en"><text>far up or off, very high, at the top</text></form></field>
    <note type="source"><form lang="en"><text>BKG: 52 occurrences, first LEV.14.7; Childs 2000, p. 308: pɔ́</text></form></note>
    <note><form lang="fr"><text>levil pɔ́-pɔ́ « très loin » (Lv 14,7) ; coocoo pɔ́ « tout là-haut » (Jb 22,12).</text></form></note>
  </entry>
  <entry id="pɔlaa_1352">
    <lexical-unit><form lang="kqs"><text>pɔlaa</text></form></lexical-unit>
    <trait name="status" value="attested"/>
    <variant><form lang="kqs"><text>pɔla</text></form></variant>
    <variant><form lang="kqs"><text>pɔlanin</text></form></variant>
    <sense id="pɔlaa_1352_s1">
      <grammatical-info value="Verb"/>
      <gloss lang="fr"><text>oindre, enduire ; tremper, mouiller (Keita)</text></gloss>
      <gloss lang="en"><text>anoint; soak, wet (Keita)</text></gloss>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="4.9.5 Practice religion"/>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="1.3.3 Wet"/>
    </sense>
    <field type="southern-kissi-sense"><form lang="en"><text>soak, immerse in water</text></form></field>
    <note type="source"><form lang="en"><text>BKG: 35 occurrences, first EXO.25.6; Keita 1979, p. 113: Pölaa; Childs 2000, p. 310: pɔ̀ɔ̀làá</text></form></note>
    <note><form lang="fr"><text>Dans la Bible, pɔla s'emploie pour l'onction (EXO 28,41 ; 40,15).</text></form></note>
  </entry>
  <entry id="pɔ́lɔ́nndo_1353">
    <lexical-unit><form lang="kqs"><text>pɔ́lɔ́nndo</text></form></lexical-unit>
    <trait name="noun-class" value="o"/>
    <trait name="status" value="attested"/>
    <sense id="pɔ́lɔ́nndo_1353_s1">
      <grammatical-info value="Noun"/>
      <gloss lang="fr"><text>marécage</text></gloss>
      <gloss lang="en"><text>swamp, marsh</text></gloss>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="1.3.1 Bodies of water"/>
    </sense>
    <note type="source"><form lang="en"><text>BKG: 3 occurrences, first PSA.40.3; Keita 1979, p. 155: Pölönndo</text></form></note>
  </entry>
  <entry id="pɔmbɔɔ_1354">
    <lexical-unit><form lang="kqs"><text>pɔmbɔɔ</text></form></lexical-unit>
    <trait name="noun-class" value="o"/>
    <trait name="status" value="attested"/>
    <field type="plural"><form lang="kqs"><text>pɔmbɔa</text></form></field>
    <variant><form lang="kqs"><text>pɔmbɔ</text></form></variant>
    <sense id="pɔmbɔɔ_1354_s1">
      <grammatical-info value="Noun"/>
      <gloss lang="fr"><text>cadet, frère ou sœur cadet(te) ; petit</text></gloss>
      <gloss lang="en"><text>younger sibling; small, lesser</text></gloss>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="4.1.9 Kinship"/>
    </sense>
    <field type="southern-kissi-sense"><form lang="en"><text>small</text></form></field>
    <note type="source"><form lang="en"><text>BKG: 155 occurrences, first GEN.1.16; Keita 1979, p. 134: Pömböö; Childs 2000, p. 309: pɔ̀mbɔ̀-</text></form></note>
  </entry>
  <entry id="pɔmndo_1355">
    <lexical-unit><form lang="kqs"><text>pɔmndo</text></form></lexical-unit>
    <trait name="noun-class" value="o"/>
    <trait name="status" value="attested"/>
    <field type="plural"><form lang="kqs"><text>pɔmndan</text></form></field>
    <sense id="pɔmndo_1355_s1">
      <grammatical-info value="Noun"/>
      <gloss lang="fr"><text>ruine (de ville), lieu dévasté</text></gloss>
      <gloss lang="en"><text>ruin, ruined town</text></gloss>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="7.9.3 Destroy"/>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="6.5.1 Building"/>
    </sense>
    <field type="southern-kissi-sense"><form lang="en"><text>a deserted or abandoned town, former town site</text></form></field>
    <note type="source"><form lang="en"><text>BKG: 8 occurrences, first DEU.13.17; Childs 2000, p. 309: pɔ̀mndó</text></form></note>
    <note><form lang="fr"><text>ciee pɔmndo « un monceau de ruines » (Jos 8,28) ; kobila … la siŋnun pɔmndan « vos villes deviendront des ruines » (Lv 26,33).</text></form></note>
  </entry>
  <entry id="pɔnɔɔ_1356">
    <lexical-unit><form lang="kqs"><text>pɔnɔɔ</text></form></lexical-unit>
    <trait name="noun-class" value="o"/>
    <trait name="status" value="attested"/>
    <sense id="pɔnɔɔ_1356_s1">
      <grammatical-info value="Noun"/>
      <gloss lang="fr"><text>époux, mari</text></gloss>
      <gloss lang="en"><text>husband</text></gloss>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="4.1.9 Kinship"/>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="2.6.1 Marriage"/>
    </sense>
    <note type="source"><form lang="en"><text>BKG: 24 occurrences, first EXO.21.22; Keita 1979, p. 134: Pönöö; Childs 2000, p. 309: pɔ́nɔ̀ɔ́</text></form></note>
  </entry>
  <entry id="pɔtɔlla_1357">
    <lexical-unit><form lang="kqs"><text>pɔtɔlla</text></form></lexical-unit>
    <trait name="status" value="attested"/>
    <variant><form lang="kqs"><text>pɔtɔlten</text></form></variant>
    <variant><form lang="kqs"><text>pɔtɔlaa</text></form></variant>
    <variant><form lang="kqs"><text>pɔtɔlte</text></form></variant>
    <sense id="pɔtɔlla_1357_s1">
      <grammatical-info value="Noun"/>
      <gloss lang="fr"><text>travailleurs forcés, corvéables ; (pɔtɔlten) corvée, servitude</text></gloss>
      <gloss lang="en"><text>forced labourers; (pɔtɔlten) forced labour, servitude</text></gloss>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="6.1.1 Worker"/>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="4.5 Authority"/>
    </sense>
    <note type="source"><form lang="en"><text>BKG: 5 occurrences, first GEN.47.21</text></form></note>
    <note><form lang="fr"><text>Pluriel ; le singulier n'est pas relevé. siinguu … pɔtɔlla « réduire en servitude » (Gn 47,21) ; Hadoram va pɔtɔlla bollen « Adoram était chef des corvées » (2 S 20,24).</text></form></note>
  </entry>
  <entry id="pɔw_1358">
    <lexical-unit><form lang="kqs"><text>pɔw</text></form></lexical-unit>
    <trait name="status" value="attested"/>
    <sense id="pɔw_1358_s1">
      <grammatical-info value="Verb"/>
      <gloss lang="fr"><text>s'égarer, se tromper ; être en faute</text></gloss>
      <gloss lang="en"><text>go astray, err; be at fault</text></gloss>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="4.3 Behavior"/>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="7.6.3 Lose, misplace"/>
    </sense>
    <note type="source"><form lang="en"><text>BKG: 24 occurrences, first EXO.14.3</text></form></note>
    <note><form lang="fr"><text>Israɛlla pɔw nɛiyo « les Israélites errent (ont perdu leur chemin) » (Ex 14,3) ; Ya pɔw ni « c'est moi la fautive » (1 S 25,24). Voir pɔwlan « faute ».</text></form></note>
  </entry>
  <entry id="pɔwlan_1359">
    <lexical-unit><form lang="kqs"><text>pɔwlan</text></form></lexical-unit>
    <trait name="noun-class" value="lan"/>
    <trait name="status" value="attested"/>
    <variant><form lang="kqs"><text>pɔwla</text></form></variant>
    <sense id="pɔwlan_1359_s1">
      <grammatical-info value="Noun"/>
      <gloss lang="fr"><text>égarement, faute, péché</text></gloss>
      <gloss lang="en"><text>error, wrongdoing, sin</text></gloss>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="4.3 Behavior"/>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="4.9.5 Practice religion"/>
    </sense>
    <note type="source"><form lang="en"><text>BKG: 85 occurrences, first DEU.11.16</text></form></note>
    <note><form lang="fr"><text>luɛi o pɔwlan nin « s'égarer, tomber dans l'erreur » (Dt 11,16) ; pɔwla Yeroboam « les péchés de Jéroboam » (2 R 10,31). Voir pɔw « s'égarer ».</text></form></note>
  </entry>
  <entry id="pɔɔ_1360">
    <lexical-unit><form lang="kqs"><text>pɔɔ</text></form></lexical-unit>
    <trait name="status" value="attested"/>
    <sense id="pɔɔ_1360_s1">
      <grammatical-info value="Adverb"/>
      <gloss lang="fr"><text>d'abord, un moment, en attendant</text></gloss>
      <gloss lang="en"><text>first, for a while, meanwhile</text></gloss>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="8.4.5 Relative time"/>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="8.4.2 Take time"/>
    </sense>
    <note type="source"><form lang="en"><text>BKG: 40 occurrences, first GEN.27.44</text></form></note>
    <note><form lang="fr"><text>Kɔ mà kɔ va pɔɔ lon « va et reste là-bas quelque temps » (Gn 27,44) ; hiow ya pɔɔ laci « passe devant moi » (Gn 33,14) ; yɔngu ya pɔɔ landei pum « donne-moi d'abord un gage » (Gn 38,17).</text></form></note>
  </entry>
  <entry id="pɔɔli_1361">
    <lexical-unit><form lang="kqs"><text>pɔɔli</text></form></lexical-unit>
    <trait name="status" value="attested"/>
    <sense id="pɔɔli_1361_s1">
      <grammatical-info value="Adverb"/>
      <gloss lang="fr"><text>de loin, à distance, là-bas</text></gloss>
      <gloss lang="en"><text>from afar, at a distance, over there</text></gloss>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="8.2.6 Distance"/>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="8.5.1 Here, there"/>
    </sense>
    <note type="source"><form lang="en"><text>BKG: 7 occurrences, first JDG.4.11</text></form></note>
    <note><form lang="fr"><text>a lo levil pɔɔli « de loin tu perçois » (Ps 139,2) ; N lo coocoo pɔɔli « du haut du ciel » (Jg 5,20).</text></form></note>
  </entry>
  <entry id="pɔɔliaa_1362">
    <lexical-unit><form lang="kqs"><text>pɔɔliaa</text></form></lexical-unit>
    <trait name="status" value="attested"/>
    <variant><form lang="kqs"><text>pɔɔliaanin</text></form></variant>
    <variant><form lang="kqs"><text>pɔɔla</text></form></variant>
    <variant><form lang="kqs"><text>pɔɔlaa</text></form></variant>
    <sense id="pɔɔliaa_1362_s1">
      <grammatical-info value="Verb"/>
      <gloss lang="fr"><text>arroser, irriguer ; (pɔɔla) mouiller, tremper</text></gloss>
      <gloss lang="en"><text>water, irrigate; (pɔɔla) wet, soak</text></gloss>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="1.3.3 Wet"/>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="6.2.4 Tend a field"/>
    </sense>
    <field type="southern-kissi-sense"><form lang="en"><text>soak, immerse in water, drench, water a plant</text></form></field>
    <note type="source"><form lang="en"><text>BKG: 22 occurrences, first GEN.2.6; Childs 2000, p. 310: pɔ̀ɔ̀làá</text></form></note>
    <note><form lang="fr"><text>mɛmma va … lɛŋnden pɔɔliaa « l'eau arrosait toute la surface du sol » (Gn 2,6) ; o pɔɔla ɲɛm mun … o kooma « il les trempera dans le sang » (Lv 14,6).</text></form></note>
  </entry>
  <entry id="pɔɛɛnndo_1363">
    <lexical-unit><form lang="kqs"><text>pɔɛɛnndo</text></form></lexical-unit>
    <trait name="status" value="check"/>
    <variant><form lang="kqs"><text>pɔɛɛn</text></form></variant>
    <sense id="pɔɛɛnndo_1363_s1">
      <grammatical-info value="Verb"/>
      <gloss lang="fr"><text>oublier</text></gloss>
      <gloss lang="en"><text>forget</text></gloss>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="3.2.6 Remember"/>
    </sense>
    <field type="southern-kissi-sense"><form lang="en"><text>forget</text></form></field>
    <note type="source"><form lang="en"><text>Keita 1979, p. 113: Pöènndo; Childs 2000, p. 310: pùɛ̀ɛ̀ŋndó</text></form></note>
    <note><form lang="fr"><text>Keita écrit pöènndo ; la Bible a le radical pɔɛɛn « oublier » (JER 30,14). La forme longue pɔɛɛnndo n'y est pas attestée.</text></form></note>
  </entry>
  <entry id="pɔɛɛnɔnndo_1364">
    <lexical-unit><form lang="kqs"><text>pɔɛɛnɔnndo</text></form></lexical-unit>
    <trait name="status" value="attested"/>
    <variant><form lang="kqs"><text>pɔɛɛnun</text></form></variant>
    <variant><form lang="kqs"><text>pɔɛɛnunnin</text></form></variant>
    <sense id="pɔɛɛnɔnndo_1364_s1">
      <grammatical-info value="Verb"/>
      <gloss lang="fr"><text>oublier ; oubli ; s'oublier (Keita)</text></gloss>
      <gloss lang="en"><text>forget; oversight; forget oneself (Keita)</text></gloss>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="3.2.6 Remember"/>
    </sense>
    <field type="southern-kissi-sense"><form lang="en"><text>forget; ignore, have nothing to do with</text></form></field>
    <note type="source"><form lang="en"><text>BKG: 12 occurrences, first GEN.43.12; Keita 1979, p. 113: Pöènnönndo; Childs 2000, p. 310: pùèèŋndɔ́</text></form></note>
    <note><form lang="fr"><text>Moyen de pɔɛɛnndo. Keita écrit pöènnönndo ; la Bible écrit pɔɛɛnɔnndo (GEN 43,12) et pɔɛɛnun « oublier » (très courant).</text></form></note>
  </entry>
  <entry id="pɛ_1365">
    <lexical-unit><form lang="kqs"><text>pɛ</text></form></lexical-unit>
    <trait name="status" value="attested"/>
    <sense id="pɛ_1365_s1">
      <grammatical-info value="Particle"/>
      <gloss lang="fr"><text>particule de condition (te … pɛ)</text></gloss>
      <gloss lang="en"><text>conditional particle (te … pɛ)</text></gloss>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="9.2.6 Particles"/>
    </sense>
    <note type="source"><form lang="en"><text>BKG: 3807 occurrences, first GEN.1.22; Childs 2000, p. 350: tè … pɛ́</text></form></note>
  </entry>
  <entry id="pɛi_1366">
    <lexical-unit><form lang="kqs"><text>pɛi</text></form></lexical-unit>
    <trait name="status" value="attested"/>
    <sense id="pɛi_1366_s1">
      <grammatical-info value="Adverb"/>
      <gloss lang="fr"><text>avant-hier ; auparavant</text></gloss>
      <gloss lang="en"><text>the day before yesterday; formerly</text></gloss>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="8.4.5 Relative time"/>
    </sense>
    <note type="source"><form lang="en"><text>BKG: 6 occurrences, first GEN.42.35; Keita 1979, p. 152: Pèi</text></form></note>
    <note><form lang="fr"><text>Dans la Bible, « auparavant, autrefois » (2TI.3.14, ACT.21.38).</text></form></note>
  </entry>
  <entry id="pɛndunɔɔ_1367">
    <lexical-unit><form lang="kqs"><text>pɛndunɔɔ</text></form></lexical-unit>
    <trait name="noun-class" value="o"/>
    <trait name="status" value="attested"/>
    <field type="plural"><form lang="kqs"><text>pɛndua</text></form></field>
    <sense id="pɛndunɔɔ_1367_s1">
      <grammatical-info value="Noun"/>
      <gloss lang="fr"><text>jumeau, jumelle</text></gloss>
      <gloss lang="en"><text>twin</text></gloss>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="4.1.9 Kinship"/>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="2.6.3 Birth"/>
    </sense>
    <note type="source"><form lang="en"><text>BKG: 1 occurrences, first GEN.38.28; Keita 1979, p. 134: Pèndunöö; Childs 2000, p. 296: pɛ̀ndùnɔ̀ɔ́</text></form></note>
  </entry>
  <entry id="pɛngiaalen_1368">
    <lexical-unit><form lang="kqs"><text>pɛngiaalen</text></form></lexical-unit>
    <trait name="noun-class" value="len"/>
    <trait name="status" value="attested"/>
    <sense id="pɛngiaalen_1368_s1">
      <grammatical-info value="Noun"/>
      <gloss lang="fr"><text>repos ; (paale pɛngiaalen) jour du sabbat</text></gloss>
      <gloss lang="en"><text>rest; (paale pɛngiaalen) sabbath day</text></gloss>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="2.4.5 Rest"/>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="4.9.5 Practice religion"/>
    </sense>
    <note type="source"><form lang="en"><text>BKG: 109 occurrences, first GEN.2.3</text></form></note>
  </entry>
  <entry id="pɛngio_1369">
    <lexical-unit><form lang="kqs"><text>pɛngio</text></form></lexical-unit>
    <trait name="status" value="attested"/>
    <variant><form lang="kqs"><text>pɛngi</text></form></variant>
    <variant><form lang="kqs"><text>pɛnginin</text></form></variant>
    <sense id="pɛngio_1369_s1">
      <grammatical-info value="Verb"/>
      <gloss lang="fr"><text>se reposer ; cesser ; cesser, arrêter</text></gloss>
      <gloss lang="en"><text>rest; cease ; rest; stop, cease</text></gloss>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="2.4.5 Rest"/>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="8.4.6 Aspectual time"/>
    </sense>
    <field type="southern-kissi-sense"><form lang="en"><text>stop an activity, rest</text></form></field>
    <note type="source"><form lang="en"><text>BKG: 88 occurrences, first GEN.24.11; Keita 1979, p. 113: Pèngioo; Childs 2000, p. 297: pɛ̀ŋgìó</text></form></note>
    <note><form lang="fr"><text>Keita écrit pèngioo ; la Bible écrit pɛngio (GEN 24,11). pɛngi signifie aussi « cesser » (EXO 9,29).</text></form></note>
  </entry>
  <entry id="pɛngɛi_1370">
    <lexical-unit><form lang="kqs"><text>pɛngɛi</text></form></lexical-unit>
    <trait name="noun-class" value="i"/>
    <trait name="status" value="attested"/>
    <field type="plural"><form lang="kqs"><text>pɛngɛn</text></form></field>
    <sense id="pɛngɛi_1370_s1">
      <grammatical-info value="Noun"/>
      <gloss lang="fr"><text>planche ; bois (matériau)</text></gloss>
      <gloss lang="en"><text>board, plank; timber</text></gloss>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="6.5.3 Building materials"/>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="6.6.3 Working with wood"/>
    </sense>
    <field type="southern-kissi-sense"><form lang="en"><text>plank, board, lumber in general; also a strip of cloth, a wooden knife</text></form></field>
    <note type="source"><form lang="en"><text>BKG: 37 occurrences, first EXO.26.16; Childs 2000, p. 297: pèŋgéí</text></form></note>
  </entry>
  <entry id="pɛngɛlaa_1371">
    <lexical-unit><form lang="kqs"><text>pɛngɛlaa</text></form></lexical-unit>
    <trait name="status" value="attested"/>
    <variant><form lang="kqs"><text>pɛngɛla</text></form></variant>
    <variant><form lang="kqs"><text>pɛngɛliaa</text></form></variant>
    <sense id="pɛngɛlaa_1371_s1">
      <grammatical-info value="Verb"/>
      <gloss lang="fr"><text>étendre, étaler (un tissu sur qqch.)</text></gloss>
      <gloss lang="en"><text>spread out (a cloth over something)</text></gloss>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="7.3.7 Cover"/>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="7.3.2 Move something in a direction"/>
    </sense>
    <field type="southern-kissi-sense"><form lang="en"><text>spread out (e.g. cloth to dry); also make a matter big</text></form></field>
    <note type="source"><form lang="en"><text>BKG: 5 occurrences, first DEU.22.17; Childs 2000, p. 297: pɛ̀ŋgɛ̀làá</text></form></note>
    <note><form lang="fr"><text>pɛngɛliaa (Pr 7,16 ; Mt 21,8 « étendre des vêtements sur le chemin ») semble en être la forme plurielle ou intensive.</text></form></note>
  </entry>
  <entry id="pɛngɛlanndo_1372">
    <lexical-unit><form lang="kqs"><text>pɛngɛlanndo</text></form></lexical-unit>
    <trait name="status" value="attested"/>
    <variant><form lang="kqs"><text>pɛngɛlan</text></form></variant>
    <variant><form lang="kqs"><text>pɛngɛlannin</text></form></variant>
    <sense id="pɛngɛlanndo_1372_s1">
      <grammatical-info value="Verb"/>
      <gloss lang="fr"><text>s'étendre, se répandre</text></gloss>
      <gloss lang="en"><text>spread, extend (itself)</text></gloss>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="8.2 Big"/>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="7.2 Move"/>
    </sense>
    <field type="southern-kissi-sense"><form lang="en"><text>spread oneself out</text></form></field>
    <note type="source"><form lang="en"><text>BKG: 6 occurrences, first GEN.47.13; Childs 2000, p. 297: pɛ̀ŋgɛ̀lăŋndó</text></form></note>
    <note><form lang="fr"><text>Moyen de pɛngɛlaa : sɔŋndo … pɛngɛlan « la tache s'est étendue » (Lv 13,51).</text></form></note>
  </entry>
  <entry id="pɛŋnden_1373">
    <lexical-unit><form lang="kqs"><text>pɛŋnden</text></form></lexical-unit>
    <trait name="noun-class" value="len"/>
    <trait name="status" value="attested"/>
    <variant><form lang="kqs"><text>pɛŋnde</text></form></variant>
    <sense id="pɛŋnden_1373_s1">
      <grammatical-info value="Noun"/>
      <gloss lang="fr"><text>manque, besoin, pauvreté</text></gloss>
      <gloss lang="en"><text>want, need, poverty</text></gloss>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="6.8.1 Have wealth"/>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="4.4.2 Trouble"/>
    </sense>
    <field type="southern-kissi-sense"><form lang="en"><text>lack, need, poverty; also state of being jammed</text></form></field>
    <note type="source"><form lang="en"><text>BKG: 20 occurrences, first LEV.25.35; Childs 2000, p. 297: pɛ̀ŋndéŋ</text></form></note>
    <note><form lang="fr"><text>pɛŋnde ɲɛdiaa « manque de pain, famine » (Am 8,11).</text></form></note>
  </entry>
  <entry id="pɛɛkoo_1374">
    <lexical-unit><form lang="kqs"><text>pɛɛkoo</text></form></lexical-unit>
    <trait name="status" value="attested"/>
    <variant><form lang="kqs"><text>pɛɛku</text></form></variant>
    <variant><form lang="kqs"><text>pɛɛkaa</text></form></variant>
    <sense id="pɛɛkoo_1374_s1">
      <grammatical-info value="Verb"/>
      <gloss lang="fr"><text>enseigner</text></gloss>
      <gloss lang="en"><text>teach</text></gloss>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="3.6 Teach"/>
    </sense>
    <field type="southern-kissi-sense"><form lang="en"><text>teach; also study, learn</text></form></field>
    <note type="source"><form lang="en"><text>BKG: 180 occurrences, first EXO.35.34; Childs 2000, p. 294: pèèkɔ̀ɔ́</text></form></note>
    <note><form lang="fr"><text>vana pɛɛkaa « enseignant, maître » ; vanaa pɛɛkaa latɔŋnda « les maîtres de la loi ».</text></form></note>
  </entry>
  <entry id="pɛɛkula_1375">
    <lexical-unit><form lang="kqs"><text>pɛɛkula</text></form></lexical-unit>
    <trait name="status" value="attested"/>
    <sense id="pɛɛkula_1375_s1">
      <grammatical-info value="Noun"/>
      <gloss lang="fr"><text>enseignements, préceptes</text></gloss>
      <gloss lang="en"><text>teachings, precepts</text></gloss>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="3.6 Teach"/>
    </sense>
    <field type="southern-kissi-sense"><form lang="en"><text>teachings; ways of learning</text></form></field>
    <note type="source"><form lang="en"><text>BKG: 48 occurrences, first LEV.25.18; Childs 2000, p. 294: pèèkùláŋ</text></form></note>
  </entry>
  <entry id="pɛɛliaa_1376">
    <lexical-unit><form lang="kqs"><text>pɛɛliaa</text></form></lexical-unit>
    <trait name="status" value="attested"/>
    <variant><form lang="kqs"><text>pɛɛliaanin</text></form></variant>
    <sense id="pɛɛliaa_1376_s1">
      <grammatical-info value="Verb"/>
      <gloss lang="fr"><text>rugir, gronder (lion, tonnerre) ; hurler (chiens)</text></gloss>
      <gloss lang="en"><text>roar, rumble (lion, thunder); howl (dogs)</text></gloss>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="1.6.4 Animal actions"/>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="1.1.3 Weather"/>
    </sense>
    <note type="source"><form lang="en"><text>BKG: 21 occurrences, first 2SA.22.16</text></form></note>
  </entry>
  <entry id="pɛɛlunɔɔ_1377">
    <lexical-unit><form lang="kqs"><text>pɛɛlunɔɔ</text></form></lexical-unit>
    <trait name="noun-class" value="o"/>
    <trait name="status" value="respelled"/>
    <sense id="pɛɛlunɔɔ_1377_s1">
      <grammatical-info value="Noun"/>
      <gloss lang="fr"><text>prêtre</text></gloss>
      <gloss lang="en"><text>priest</text></gloss>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="4.9.7 Religious organization"/>
    </sense>
    <note type="source"><form lang="en"><text>Keita 1979, p. 150: Pèèlunöö</text></form></note>
    <note><form lang="fr"><text>La Bible dit vana-solia-lasálàá « prêtre ».</text></form></note>
  </entry>
  <entry id="pɛɛlɛnnden_1378">
    <lexical-unit><form lang="kqs"><text>pɛɛlɛnnden</text></form></lexical-unit>
    <trait name="noun-class" value="len"/>
    <trait name="status" value="respelled"/>
    <sense id="pɛɛlɛnnden_1378_s1">
      <grammatical-info value="Noun"/>
      <gloss lang="fr"><text>cache-sexe</text></gloss>
      <gloss lang="en"><text>loincloth</text></gloss>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="5.3.3 Traditional clothing"/>
    </sense>
    <note type="source"><form lang="en"><text>Keita 1979, p. 144: Pèèlènnden</text></form></note>
  </entry>
  <entry id="pɛɛn_1379">
    <lexical-unit><form lang="kqs"><text>pɛɛn</text></form></lexical-unit>
    <trait name="status" value="attested"/>
    <sense id="pɛɛn_1379_s1">
      <grammatical-info value="Particle"/>
      <gloss lang="fr"><text>c'est-à-dire, à savoir (particule d'apposition)</text></gloss>
      <gloss lang="en"><text>namely, that is (appositive particle)</text></gloss>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="9.2.6 Particles"/>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="9.6.3 Discourse markers"/>
    </sense>
    <note type="source"><form lang="en"><text>BKG: 1262 occurrences, first GEN.4.2</text></form></note>
    <note><form lang="fr"><text>Suit un groupe qui précise le précédent : Abɛl, pɔmbɔɔ Kain pɛɛn « Abel, le cadet de Caïn » (Gn 4,2) ; koovan pɛɛn « c'est-à-dire son sang » (Gn 9,4).</text></form></note>
  </entry>
  <entry id="pɛɛngaa_1380">
    <lexical-unit><form lang="kqs"><text>pɛɛngaa</text></form></lexical-unit>
    <trait name="status" value="attested"/>
    <variant><form lang="kqs"><text>pɛɛnga</text></form></variant>
    <variant><form lang="kqs"><text>pɛɛngaalan</text></form></variant>
    <sense id="pɛɛngaa_1380_s1">
      <grammatical-info value="Verb"/>
      <gloss lang="fr"><text>déployer (les ailes), planer ; s'ouvrir (fleur)</text></gloss>
      <gloss lang="en"><text>spread (wings), hover; open (of flowers)</text></gloss>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="1.6.4 Animal actions"/>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="7.2.1 Manner of movement"/>
    </sense>
    <note type="source"><form lang="en"><text>BKG: 2 occurrences, first GEN.1.2</text></form></note>
    <note><form lang="fr"><text>Kɔl Hala-o va o pɛɛngaa o mɛmma man coo « l'Esprit de Dieu planait au-dessus des eaux » (Gn 1,2) ; peengela pɛɛngaalan « fleurs épanouies » (1 R 6,32).</text></form></note>
  </entry>
  <entry id="pɛɛngio_1381">
    <lexical-unit><form lang="kqs"><text>pɛɛngio</text></form></lexical-unit>
    <trait name="status" value="check"/>
    <sense id="pɛɛngio_1381_s1">
      <grammatical-info value="Verb"/>
      <gloss lang="fr"><text>cesser</text></gloss>
      <gloss lang="en"><text>cease, stop</text></gloss>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="8.4.6 Aspectual time"/>
    </sense>
    <note type="source"><form lang="en"><text>Keita 1979, p. 113: Pèèngio</text></form></note>
    <note><form lang="fr"><text>Non trouvé dans la Bible, qui emploie pɛngi pour « cesser » ; peut-être le même verbe que pɛngio.</text></form></note>
  </entry>
  <entry id="pɛɛngulan_1382">
    <lexical-unit><form lang="kqs"><text>pɛɛngulan</text></form></lexical-unit>
    <trait name="noun-class" value="lan"/>
    <trait name="status" value="attested"/>
    <variant><form lang="kqs"><text>pɛɛngula</text></form></variant>
    <variant><form lang="kqs"><text>pɛngulan</text></form></variant>
    <sense id="pɛɛngulan_1382_s1">
      <grammatical-info value="Noun"/>
      <gloss lang="fr"><text>différence, séparation ; limite, frontière</text></gloss>
      <gloss lang="en"><text>difference, distinction; boundary, border</text></gloss>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="4.6.7 Region"/>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="8.6.6 Edge"/>
    </sense>
    <note type="source"><form lang="en"><text>BKG: 98 occurrences, first GEN.1.7; Keita 1979, p. 148: Pèngulan</text></form></note>
    <note><form lang="fr"><text>Dans la Bible : sina pɛngulan « faire la différence » (Lv 20,25 ; Ez 22,26). Graphie principale pɛɛngulan (98 occurrences), rarement pɛngulan.</text></form></note>
  </entry>
  <entry id="pɛɛpɛi_1383">
    <lexical-unit><form lang="kqs"><text>pɛɛpɛi</text></form></lexical-unit>
    <trait name="status" value="respelled"/>
    <field type="plural"><form lang="kqs"><text>pɛɛpɛɛlan</text></form></field>
    <sense id="pɛɛpɛi_1383_s1">
      <grammatical-info value="Noun"/>
      <gloss lang="fr"><text>nageoire</text></gloss>
      <gloss lang="en"><text>fin</text></gloss>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="1.6.2 Parts of an animal"/>
    </sense>
    <note type="source"><form lang="en"><text>Keita 1979, p. 137: Pèèpèi</text></form></note>
    <note><form lang="fr"><text>La Bible a le pluriel pɛɛpɛɛlan (LEV.11.9, DEU.14.9) ; le singulier est réécrit d'après Keita.</text></form></note>
  </entry>
  <entry id="pɛɛsaa_1384">
    <lexical-unit><form lang="kqs"><text>pɛɛsaa</text></form></lexical-unit>
    <trait name="status" value="attested"/>
    <variant><form lang="kqs"><text>pɛɛsa</text></form></variant>
    <sense id="pɛɛsaa_1384_s1">
      <grammatical-info value="Verb"/>
      <gloss lang="fr"><text>mépriser, dédaigner</text></gloss>
      <gloss lang="en"><text>despise, scorn</text></gloss>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="3.4.2 Feel bad"/>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="4.3 Behavior"/>
    </sense>
    <field type="southern-kissi-sense"><form lang="en"><text>oversee; blame, criticize</text></form></field>
    <note type="source"><form lang="en"><text>BKG: 24 occurrences, first NUM.14.11; Childs 2000, p. 295: pèèsàá</text></form></note>
  </entry>
  <entry id="rɛsɛnndo_1385">
    <lexical-unit><form lang="kqs"><text>rɛsɛnndo</text></form></lexical-unit>
    <trait name="status" value="attested"/>
    <variant><form lang="kqs"><text>rɛsɛn</text></form></variant>
    <variant><form lang="kqs"><text>rɛsɛnndon</text></form></variant>
    <variant><form lang="kqs"><text>rɛsɛŋun</text></form></variant>
    <variant><form lang="kqs"><text>rɛsɛnndan</text></form></variant>
    <variant><form lang="kqs"><text>rɛsɛnnda</text></form></variant>
    <sense id="rɛsɛnndo_1385_s1">
      <grammatical-info value="Noun"/>
      <gloss lang="fr"><text>vigne, cep de vigne ; (rɛsɛnndon) raisins</text></gloss>
      <gloss lang="en"><text>vine, grapevine; (rɛsɛnndon) grapes</text></gloss>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="1.5.3 Grass, herb, vine"/>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="6.2.1 Growing crops"/>
    </sense>
    <note type="source"><form lang="en"><text>BKG: 41 occurrences, first GEN.9.20</text></form></note>
    <note><form lang="fr"><text>rɛsɛŋun toaŋaa « raisins secs » (Ct 2,5) ; n'rɛsɛnndan « vignes, vignobles ».</text></form></note>
  </entry>
