      <gloss lang="fr"><text>(idéophone) tout à fait ; d'un rouge vif (lasiaŋa vaŋ, diw vaŋ)</text></gloss>
      <gloss lang="en"><text>(ideophone) completely; bright red (lasiaŋa vaŋ, diw vaŋ)</text></gloss>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="9.2.8 Ideophones"/>
    </sense>
    <note type="source"><form lang="en"><text>BKG: 7 occurrences, first EXO.11.1</text></form></note>
  </entry>
  <entry id="veeloo_1807">
    <lexical-unit><form lang="kqs"><text>veeloo</text></form></lexical-unit>
    <trait name="status" value="attested"/>
    <variant><form lang="kqs"><text>veelu</text></form></variant>
    <variant><form lang="kqs"><text>veelunin</text></form></variant>
    <sense id="veeloo_1807_s1">
      <grammatical-info value="Verb"/>
      <gloss lang="fr"><text>appeler ; invoquer</text></gloss>
      <gloss lang="en"><text>call ; call; call upon</text></gloss>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="3.5.1 Say"/>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="4.9.5 Practice religion"/>
    </sense>
    <field type="southern-kissi-sense"><form lang="en"><text>call, name</text></form></field>
    <note type="source"><form lang="en"><text>BKG: 127 occurrences, first GEN.4.26; Keita 1979, p. 114: Veeluo; Childs 2000, p. 382: wèèlòó</text></form></note>
    <note><form lang="fr"><text>Keita écrit veeluo ; la Bible écrit veeloo (GEN 4,26).</text></form></note>
  </entry>
  <entry id="veeluanndo_1808">
    <lexical-unit><form lang="kqs"><text>veeluanndo</text></form></lexical-unit>
    <trait name="status" value="respelled"/>
    <sense id="veeluanndo_1808_s1">
      <grammatical-info value="Verb"/>
      <gloss lang="fr"><text>s'interpeller</text></gloss>
      <gloss lang="en"><text>call one another</text></gloss>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="3.5.1 Say"/>
    </sense>
    <note type="source"><form lang="en"><text>Keita 1979, p. 114: Veeluanndo</text></form></note>
    <note><form lang="fr"><text>Réciproque de veeloo.</text></form></note>
  </entry>
  <entry id="veelɔnndo_1809">
    <lexical-unit><form lang="kqs"><text>veelɔnndo</text></form></lexical-unit>
    <trait name="status" value="attested"/>
    <sense id="veelɔnndo_1809_s1">
      <grammatical-info value="Verb"/>
      <gloss lang="fr"><text>être appelé, s'appeler</text></gloss>
      <gloss lang="en"><text>be called, be named</text></gloss>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="3.5.1 Say"/>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="9.7 Name"/>
    </sense>
    <field type="southern-kissi-sense"><form lang="en"><text>call oneself</text></form></field>
    <note type="source"><form lang="en"><text>BKG: 13 occurrences, first JER.7.10; Childs 2000, p. 382: wèèlɔ̌ŋndó</text></form></note>
    <note><form lang="fr"><text>Moyen de veeloo.</text></form></note>
  </entry>
  <entry id="veesiaa_1810">
    <lexical-unit><form lang="kqs"><text>veesiaa</text></form></lexical-unit>
    <trait name="status" value="attested"/>
    <sense id="veesiaa_1810_s1">
      <grammatical-info value="Verb"/>
      <gloss lang="fr"><text>faire sécher, dessécher</text></gloss>
      <gloss lang="en"><text>make dry, wither</text></gloss>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="1.3.3 Wet"/>
    </sense>
    <note type="source"><form lang="en"><text>BKG: 28 occurrences, first GEN.41.6; Keita 1979, p. 114: Veesiaa</text></form></note>
    <note><form lang="fr"><text>Causatif de vesaa (GEN 41,6).</text></form></note>
  </entry>
  <entry id="velaa_1811">
    <lexical-unit><form lang="kqs"><text>velaa</text></form></lexical-unit>
    <trait name="status" value="attested"/>
    <variant><form lang="kqs"><text>vela</text></form></variant>
    <variant><form lang="kqs"><text>velanin</text></form></variant>
    <sense id="velaa_1811_s1">
      <grammatical-info value="Verb"/>
      <gloss lang="fr"><text>tarir, baisser (eaux)</text></gloss>
      <gloss lang="en"><text>dry up, recede (water)</text></gloss>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="1.3.2 Movement of water"/>
    </sense>
    <field type="southern-kissi-sense"><form lang="en"><text>become dry (of water)</text></form></field>
    <note type="source"><form lang="en"><text>BKG: 5 occurrences, first GEN.8.1; Keita 1979, p. 114: Velaa; Childs 2000, p. 382: wèlàá</text></form></note>
  </entry>
  <entry id="velan_1812">
    <lexical-unit><form lang="kqs"><text>velan</text></form></lexical-unit>
    <trait name="noun-class" value="lan"/>
    <trait name="status" value="attested"/>
    <sense id="velan_1812_s1">
      <grammatical-info value="Noun"/>
      <gloss lang="fr"><text>image, ressemblance</text></gloss>
      <gloss lang="en"><text>image, likeness</text></gloss>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="8.3.1 Shape"/>
    </sense>
    <field type="southern-kissi-sense"><form lang="en"><text>resemblances (from wèlǎŋndó 'resemble')</text></form></field>
    <note type="source"><form lang="en"><text>BKG: 67 occurrences, first GEN.1.26; Childs 2000, p. 383: wèlâŋndáŋ</text></form></note>
    <note><form lang="fr"><text>Verbe apparenté vel « ressembler à » (Gn 1,26).</text></form></note>
  </entry>
  <entry id="velanndo_1813">
    <lexical-unit><form lang="kqs"><text>velanndo</text></form></lexical-unit>
    <trait name="status" value="check"/>
    <sense id="velanndo_1813_s1">
      <grammatical-info value="Verb"/>
      <gloss lang="fr"><text>se tarir (Keita) ; ressemblance, sens (Bible)</text></gloss>
      <gloss lang="en"><text>dry up (Keita); likeness, meaning (Bible)</text></gloss>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="1.3.2 Movement of water"/>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="8.3.5 Type, kind"/>
    </sense>
    <field type="southern-kissi-sense"><form lang="en"><text>resemble</text></form></field>
    <note type="source"><form lang="en"><text>Keita 1979, p. 114: Velanndo; Childs 2000, p. 383: wèlǎŋndó</text></form></note>
    <note><form lang="fr"><text>Dans la Bible, velanndo est « sens (d'un nom), ressemblance » (GEN 29,34), de vel « ressembler » ; le sens « se tarir » de Keita n'y est pas.</text></form></note>
  </entry>
  <entry id="vellaa-velle_1814">
    <lexical-unit><form lang="kqs"><text>vellaa-velle</text></form></lexical-unit>
    <trait name="status" value="attested"/>
    <sense id="vellaa-velle_1814_s1">
      <grammatical-info value="Pronoun"/>
      <gloss lang="fr"><text>l'un l'autre, les uns les autres (réciproque)</text></gloss>
      <gloss lang="en"><text>one another, each other</text></gloss>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="9.2.3 Pronouns"/>
    </sense>
    <field type="southern-kissi-sense"><form lang="en"><text>(adverb) together</text></form></field>
    <note type="source"><form lang="en"><text>BKG: 145 occurrences, first GEN.11.3; Childs 2000, p. 383: wéllàá-wèllè</text></form></note>
    <note><form lang="fr"><text>Má dimulan vellaa-velle « ils se dirent l'un à l'autre » (GEN.11.3).</text></form></note>
