      <gloss lang="en"><text>crying, weeping, wailing</text></gloss>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="3.4.2 Feel bad"/>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="3.5.1 Say"/>
    </sense>
    <field type="southern-kissi-sense"><form lang="en"><text>weeping, crying</text></form></field>
    <note type="source"><form lang="en"><text>BKG: 31 occurrences, first EXO.11.6; Childs 2000, p. 400: yééláŋ</text></form></note>
    <note><form lang="fr"><text>mɛli yeelan « crier, se lamenter ».</text></form></note>
  </entry>
  <entry id="yeelannɔɔ_1917">
    <lexical-unit><form lang="kqs"><text>yeelannɔɔ</text></form></lexical-unit>
    <trait name="noun-class" value="o"/>
    <trait name="status" value="respelled"/>
    <sense id="yeelannɔɔ_1917_s1">
      <grammatical-info value="Noun"/>
      <gloss lang="fr"><text>allié</text></gloss>
      <gloss lang="en"><text>ally</text></gloss>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="4.1.1 Friend"/>
    </sense>
    <note type="source"><form lang="en"><text>Keita 1979, p. 149: Yeelannöö</text></form></note>
  </entry>
  <entry id="yeeliaa_1918">
    <lexical-unit><form lang="kqs"><text>yeeliaa</text></form></lexical-unit>
    <trait name="status" value="attested"/>
    <sense id="yeeliaa_1918_s1">
      <grammatical-info value="Verb"/>
      <gloss lang="fr"><text>rendre agréable, rendre savoureux ; faire réussir</text></gloss>
      <gloss lang="en"><text>make pleasant or tasty; make prosper</text></gloss>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="2.3.3 Taste"/>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="4.4 Prosperity, trouble"/>
    </sense>
    <note type="source"><form lang="en"><text>BKG: 6 occurrences, first GEN.24.21</text></form></note>
    <note><form lang="fr"><text>Causatif de yeela. Mɛlɛka yeeliaa kela ndɔɔ « le Seigneur faisait réussir son voyage » (GEN.24.21).</text></form></note>
  </entry>
  <entry id="yeelɛiyo_1919">
    <lexical-unit><form lang="kqs"><text>yeelɛiyo</text></form></lexical-unit>
    <trait name="status" value="attested"/>
    <variant><form lang="kqs"><text>yeelɛi</text></form></variant>
    <variant><form lang="kqs"><text>yeelɛiyon</text></form></variant>
    <variant><form lang="kqs"><text>yeelɛilen</text></form></variant>
    <variant><form lang="kqs"><text>yeelɛilan</text></form></variant>
    <variant><form lang="kqs"><text>yeelɛin</text></form></variant>
    <variant><form lang="kqs"><text>yeelɛiya</text></form></variant>
    <sense id="yeelɛiyo_1919_s1">
      <grammatical-info value="Adjective"/>
      <gloss lang="fr"><text>savoureux, délicieux, doux ; agréable</text></gloss>
      <gloss lang="en"><text>tasty, delicious, sweet; pleasant</text></gloss>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="2.3.3 Taste"/>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="8.3.7 Good"/>
    </sense>
    <note type="source"><form lang="en"><text>BKG: 11 occurrences, first GEN.27.7</text></form></note>
    <note><form lang="fr"><text>Cf. yeela « bon, agréable ». ɲɛmahilu yeelɛiyo « un mets savoureux » (GEN.27.7).</text></form></note>
  </entry>
  <entry id="yeemaa_1920">
    <lexical-unit><form lang="kqs"><text>yeemaa</text></form></lexical-unit>
    <trait name="status" value="attested"/>
    <variant><form lang="kqs"><text>yeema</text></form></variant>
    <variant><form lang="kqs"><text>yeemanin</text></form></variant>
    <sense id="yeemaa_1920_s1">
      <grammatical-info value="Verb"/>
      <gloss lang="fr"><text>vouloir, désirer, aimer</text></gloss>
      <gloss lang="en"><text>want, desire, love</text></gloss>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="3.3 Want"/>
    </sense>
    <field type="southern-kissi-sense"><form lang="en"><text>also: need</text></form></field>
    <note type="source"><form lang="en"><text>BKG: 22 occurrences, first NUM.16.10; Childs 2000, p. 400: yèèmàá</text></form></note>
  </entry>
  <entry id="yeemɛi_1921">
    <lexical-unit><form lang="kqs"><text>yeemɛi</text></form></lexical-unit>
    <trait name="noun-class" value="i"/>
    <trait name="status" value="attested"/>
    <sense id="yeemɛi_1921_s1">
      <grammatical-info value="Noun"/>
      <gloss lang="fr"><text>désir, envie, volonté</text></gloss>
      <gloss lang="en"><text>desire, longing, will</text></gloss>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="3.3 Want"/>
    </sense>
    <field type="southern-kissi-sense"><form lang="en"><text>(adjective) wanting, in need of</text></form></field>
    <note type="source"><form lang="en"><text>BKG: 203 occurrences, first GEN.3.6; Childs 2000, p. 400: yèèmɛ̀</text></form></note>
  </entry>
  <entry id="yeiyo_1922">
    <lexical-unit><form lang="kqs"><text>yeiyo</text></form></lexical-unit>
    <trait name="status" value="attested"/>
    <variant><form lang="kqs"><text>yei</text></form></variant>
    <sense id="yeiyo_1922_s1">
      <grammatical-info value="Verb"/>
      <gloss lang="fr"><text>insulter, injurier, défier ; blasphémer</text></gloss>
      <gloss lang="en"><text>insult, revile, defy; blaspheme</text></gloss>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="3.5.1 Say"/>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="4.8 Conflict"/>
    </sense>
    <note type="source"><form lang="en"><text>BKG: 1 occurrences, first 1PE.3.9; Childs 2000, p. 401: yèìyó</text></form></note>
    <note><form lang="fr"><text>Vana yei pɛ fuɲa ndɔ « celui qui maudit son père » (MRK.7.10) ; le yei o yei vanaa cɔvaa Hala « parce qu'il a défié l'armée de Dieu » (1SA.17.36).</text></form></note>
  </entry>
  <entry id="yékén_1923">
    <lexical-unit><form lang="kqs"><text>yékén</text></form></lexical-unit>
    <trait name="status" value="attested"/>
    <sense id="yékén_1923_s1">
      <grammatical-info value="Ideophone"/>
      <gloss lang="fr"><text>(idéophone) attentivement (yaŋ nilan yékén « écouter attentivement »)</text></gloss>
      <gloss lang="en"><text>(ideophone) attentively, intently (yaŋ nilan yékén 'listen closely')</text></gloss>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="9.2.8 Ideophones"/>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="2.3.2 Hear"/>
    </sense>
    <note type="source"><form lang="en"><text>BKG: 6 occurrences, first JOB.37.14</text></form></note>
  </entry>
  <entry id="yekpandio_1924">
    <lexical-unit><form lang="kqs"><text>yekpandio</text></form></lexical-unit>
    <trait name="noun-class" value="o"/>
    <trait name="status" value="respelled"/>
    <sense id="yekpandio_1924_s1">
      <grammatical-info value="Noun"/>
      <gloss lang="fr"><text>fusil</text></gloss>
      <gloss lang="en"><text>gun</text></gloss>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="4.8.3 War"/>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="6.4.1 Hunt"/>
    </sense>
    <note type="source"><form lang="en"><text>Keita 1979, p. 156: Yekpandio; Childs 2000, p. 401: yèkpándìó</text></form></note>
  </entry>
  <entry id="yelenyelenndo_1925">
    <lexical-unit><form lang="kqs"><text>yelenyelenndo</text></form></lexical-unit>
    <trait name="status" value="attested"/>
    <variant><form lang="kqs"><text>yelenyelen</text></form></variant>
    <variant><form lang="kqs"><text>yelenyelennde</text></form></variant>
    <sense id="yelenyelenndo_1925_s1">
      <grammatical-info value="Noun"/>
      <gloss lang="fr"><text>flamme</text></gloss>
      <gloss lang="en"><text>flame</text></gloss>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="5.5 Fire"/>
    </sense>
    <note type="source"><form lang="en"><text>BKG: 5 occurrences, first NUM.21.28</text></form></note>
    <note><form lang="fr"><text>yelenyelen leyin « la flamme du feu » (JDG.13.20).</text></form></note>
  </entry>
  <entry id="yemaa_1926">
    <lexical-unit><form lang="kqs"><text>yemaa</text></form></lexical-unit>
    <trait name="noun-class" value="o"/>
    <trait name="status" value="attested"/>
    <variant><form lang="kqs"><text>yema</text></form></variant>
    <sense id="yemaa_1926_s1">
      <grammatical-info value="Noun"/>
      <gloss lang="fr"><text>sœur (d'un homme), frère (d'une femme)</text></gloss>
      <gloss lang="en"><text>opposite-sex sibling: a man's sister, a woman's brother</text></gloss>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="4.1.9 Kinship"/>
    </sense>
    <field type="southern-kissi-sense"><form lang="en"><text>sister; brother in some dialects</text></form></field>
    <note type="source"><form lang="en"><text>BKG: 39 occurrences, first GEN.24.55; Keita 1979, p. 134: Yemaa; Childs 2000, p. 402: yèmàá</text></form></note>
    <note><form lang="fr"><text>Keita : « la sœur ». Dans la Bible, Laban est aussi le yemaa de Rébecca (Gn 24,55 ; 28,5).</text></form></note>
  </entry>
  <entry id="yembuo_1927">
    <lexical-unit><form lang="kqs"><text>yembuo</text></form></lexical-unit>
    <trait name="noun-class" value="o"/>
    <trait name="status" value="respelled"/>
    <variant><form lang="kqs"><text>yembu</text></form></variant>
    <sense id="yembuo_1927_s1">
      <grammatical-info value="Noun"/>
      <gloss lang="fr"><text>célibataire</text></gloss>
      <gloss lang="en"><text>unmarried person</text></gloss>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="2.6.1 Marriage"/>
    </sense>
    <field type="southern-kissi-sense"><form lang="en"><text>unmarried adult</text></form></field>
    <note type="source"><form lang="en"><text>Keita 1979, p. 134: Yembuo; Childs 2000, p. 402: yèmbòó</text></form></note>
    <note><form lang="fr"><text>La Bible a yembu « sans être marié » (1Co 7,8).</text></form></note>
  </entry>
  <entry id="yemnde_1928">
